hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17401","320 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musa al-Anqazi, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from his father, from his grandfather: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Maghrib in the mosque of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, and when he had prayed, some people stood up to offer voluntary prayers, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to this prayer in your houses."
"17402","321 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, he said: Narrated to us Humayd ibn al-Rabi, narrated to us Dawud ibn Ata al-Madani, narrated to us Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man purifies himself in his house then goes out except that he is in prayer until he performs his prayer, so none of you should interlock his fingers while he is in prayer."
"17403","322 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Mattawayh al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari, narrated to us Salih ibn Badal, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Madani, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from his father, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man wearing a face-cover passed by us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be division and disagreement among the people, and this man and his companions will be upon the truth. Kab said: So I caught up with him and looked at him until I recognized him. And we used to ask Kab who the man was, and he would refuse to tell us, until Kab went out with Ali to Kufah and remained there until he died, and it was as though we came to know that that man was Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"17404","323 - Narrated to us Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Ramli, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Uwaysi, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Nistas (H). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, narrated to us Bishr ibn Ubays ibn Marhum al-Attar, narrated to us my grandfather Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Nistas, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to his Companions: What do you say about a man killed in the path of Allah? They said: Paradise. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise, if Allah wills. He said: What do you say about a man who dies in the path of Allah? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Paradise, if Allah wills. He said: What do you say about a man who dies and two just men stand up and say: We know nothing but good? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Paradise, if Allah wills. He said: What do you say about a man who dies and two just men stand up and say: We know no good? They said: Hellfire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A sinner, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."
"17405","324 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Bishr al-Kufi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile Ali, for he was deeply devoted in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"17406","Abd al-Malik ibn Kab ibn Ujrah from Kab. 325 - Narrated to us Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Adam ibn Abi Iyas, narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab, from his uncle Abd al-Malik, he said: I went out with Kab ibn Ujrah on the day of Eid to the prayer ground, and he sat down before the imam came and did not pray until the imam had left, while the people were going off as though in a line toward the mosque, so I said: Do you not see? He said: This is an innovation and abandonment of the Sunnah."
"17407","326 - Narrated to us Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Anas ibn Iyad, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: I attended one of the two Eids with Kab, and when the people left, most of them went to the mosque, while I saw him heading for home, so I said: O father, will you not head to the mosque, for I see the people heading to it? He said: Much of what you see is harshness and lack of knowledge; these two rakahs are the voluntary prayer of this day until the prayer calls you."
"17408","Muhammad ibn Kab ibn Ujrah from his father. 327 - Narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, my uncle narrated to me, he said: I went out with my father - and he was one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - on the day of Eid to the prayer ground, and he sat down before the imam came, and did not pray; then when the imam left, they left going toward the mosque as though in a line, so I said to him: Do you not see the people? He said: This is an innovation and abandonment of the Sunnah."
"17409","Al-Rabi ibn Kab ibn Ujrah from his father. 328 - Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, narrated to us Amr ibn al-Numan, Musa ibn Dihqan narrated to me, al-Rabi ibn Kab ibn Ujrah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: O so-and-so, have you married? He said: No. Then he said to me: Have you married? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a previously married woman? I said: No, rather a previously married woman. He said: Then why not a virgin whom you bite playfully and who bites you."
"17410","Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Kab ibn Ujrah from his grandfather. 329 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Harish, narrated to us Sufyan, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Kab: Umar asked Kab: What did Kab give as ransom when he shaved his head? He said: He slaughtered a cow."
"17411","330 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Sad, narrated to us my uncle, narrated to us my father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban al-Ansari, from Sulayman ibn Kab ibn Ujrah: Kab said to Umar: I slaughtered a cow."
"17412","Anas ibn Sulayman, freedman of Kab ibn Ujrah, from Kab. 331 - Narrated to us Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from Anas ibn Sulayman, freedman of Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: I bear witness that I saw four or five of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing saffron-dyed garments, among them Kab ibn Ujrah."
"17413","Abu Thumamah al-Hannat from Kab ibn Ujrah. 332 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz al-Basri, narrated to us Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Muadhdhin, narrated to us Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra, narrated to us Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from Abu Thumamah al-Hannat, he said: Kab ibn Ujrah met me while I was heading to the mosque with my fingers interlocked, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you performs ablution then comes to the mosque, let him not interlock his fingers, for he is in prayer."
"17414","333 - Narrated to us Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from Abu Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Thumamah, he said: I met Kab ibn Ujrah on a Friday while I was going to the Friday prayer, and when I saw him I hastened toward him with my fingers interlocked; when I drew near him he struck my hands and separated my fingers. I said: What is this, O Abu Muhammad? He said: We have been forbidden for any of us to interlock his fingers in prayer. I said: I am not in prayer. He said: Have you not performed ablution while intending the Friday prayer? I said: Yes. He said: Then you are in prayer."
"17415","Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Kab ibn Ujrah. 334 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Sufyan (H). And narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perform ablution then go out heading deliberately to the mosque, do not interlock your fingers, for you are in prayer."
"17416","335 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt and Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from a man of the family of Kab ibn Ujrah, from Kab ibn Ujrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Kab, when you leave your house intending prayer, do not interlock your fingers."
"17417","336 - Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, narrated to us Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you perform ablution and perform it well, then go out heading deliberately to the mosque, do not interlock your fingers."
"17418","337 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abu Mashar, from Abu Said al-Maqburi, from a man of Banu Salimah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Kab ibn Ujrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man performs ablution in his house then goes out intending prayer except that he is in prayer until he completes his prayer, so let him not interlock his fingers in prayer."
"17419","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Kab ibn Ujrah. 339 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Kab ibn Ujrah: He slaughtered a cow."
"17420","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn from Kab ibn Ujrah. 340 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Ibn al-Asbahani, narrated to us Sharik, from Jabir, from Abu Jafar, he said: I said to Kab ibn Ujrah: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard him say: The daughter of the brother and the daughter of the sister through breastfeeding are not lawful."
"17421","Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad from Kab ibn Ujrah. 341 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan, narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam (H). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Kathir - both said: Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Abu Ishaq, from a man called Abu Bakr, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we have learned how to greet you with peace, but how do we invoke blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"17422","342 - Narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Israil, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How do we invoke blessings upon you? Then he mentioned the like of it."
"17423","Abdullah ibn Abi al-Husayn from Kab ibn Ujrah. 343 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Husayn, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to the best character of the people of this world and the Hereafter? Joining ties with the one who cuts you off, pardoning the one who wrongs you, and giving to the one who deprives you. Luwayn said: It is said, and Allah knows best: Abdullah ibn Abi al-Husayn, whose kunyah is Abu al-Husayn. And Abu al-Ahwas narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and he did not mention Kab ibn Ujrah."
"17424","Al-Miswar ibn Rifah al-Qurazi from Kab ibn Ujrah. 344 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abbud al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amr, from al-Miswar ibn Rifah al-Qurazi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: I witnessed two gatherings with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); as for one of them, a funeral bier was brought and it was said: This is so-and-so, and what an evil man! And evil was spoken of him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know that? They said: Yes. He said: It has become incumbent. And as for the other, the bier of a man was brought and they said: This is so-and-so, and they praised him with good, so he said: Do you know that? They said: Yes. He said: It has become incumbent."
"17425","Hudayr, freedman of Zaynab bint Jahsh, from Kab. 345 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali, narrated to us Mutamir ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Layth, from al-Hudayr - a freedman of Zaynab bint Jahsh - from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were nine, among us six non-Arabs, and said: There will be rulers; whoever believes them in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing and carries out their scheming for them is not of me nor am I of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin."
"17426","Abu Yahya, freedman of Jadah ibn Hubayrah, from Kab ibn Ujrah. 346 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli, from al-Amash, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Yahya, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until one man manages the affairs of fifty women."
"17427","Yahya ibn Jadah ibn Hubayrah from Kab ibn Ujrah. 347 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani, narrated to us Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Jadah, from Kab ibn Ujrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Kab ibn Ujrah to shave his head because of lice, then said: Fast three days, or feed six poor persons two mudds each, or slaughter."
"17428","348 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Jadah, from Kab ibn Ujrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to shave his head because of lice, and said: Fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or slaughter."
"17429","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Kab ibn Ujrah. 349 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Ismail ibn Zakariyya al-Kufi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, from Ata, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The vermin of my head harmed me, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Then whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of the head, a ransom of fasting or charity or sacrifice. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: Do you have a faraq to distribute among six poor persons - and the faraq is three sas - or a sacrifice of a sheep, or fast three days? I said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me! He said: Feed six poor persons."
"17430","Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi from Kab ibn Ujrah. 350 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Taghlibi, narrated to us Shuayb al-Anmati, from Layth, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a believer of a distress, Allah will relieve him of a distress on the Day of Resurrection; whoever conceals the fault of a believer, Allah will conceal his fault; and whoever removes a distress from a believer, Allah will remove a distress from him."
"17431","351 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Bakr ibn Khalaf (H). And narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Harish - both said: Narrated to us Rawh ibn Ubadah, narrated to us Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, he said: I heard Kab ibn Ujrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to shave my head and to ransom with a sheep."
"17432","352 - Narrated to us al-Numan ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Nafi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me, when lice harmed me, to shave my head, then fast three days or feed six poor persons, and he knew that I did not have anything with which to offer a sacrifice."
"17433","Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban from Kab. 353 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman, from Abu Mashar, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrated to me, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm came to Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban and said to him: O Abu Hafs, narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there is no disagreement! So he narrated from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits with him he is immersed in it. He said: He says to his Companions: Intercede for us, if Allah wills."
"17434","Abu Abi Musa al-Hilali of Basrah from Kab ibn Ujrah. 354 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, Abu Musa al-Hilali narrated to me, from his father, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: Who is here? Do you hear? After me there will be rulers who act in disobedience to Allah; whoever shares in their deeds and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me nor am I of him, and whoever does not share in their deeds nor help them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him."
"17435","Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Basri from Kab ibn Ujrah. 355 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi reported to us, Haddathani Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from Aban ibn Salih that he heard al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan say: I asked Kab ibn Ujrah - I said: Concerning you was revealed the verse of concession, so what did you do? He said: I slaughtered a sheep."
"17436","356 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani, narrated to us Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan: Kab ibn Ujrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: There will be rulers over you after me who speak wisdom upon pulpits, but when they descend it is snatched from them, and their hearts are fouler than corpses. Whoever believes them in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me nor am I of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin; and whoever does not believe them in their lies nor help them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin."
"17437","357 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Asbahani, my father narrated to me, narrated to us al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam, narrated to us Abu Salamah al-Sarraj, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hasan, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire."
"17438","358 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Uqayli al-Asbahani, my father narrated to me, narrated to us al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam, narrated to us Abu Salamah al-Sarraj, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hasan, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Kab ibn Ujrah, may Allah protect you from rulers who will come after me; whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me nor am I of him, and he will never come to me at the Basin."
"17439","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Kab ibn Ujrah. 359 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Abu Shihab, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he mentioned a tribulation and drew it near, then a man wearing a face-cover passed, so he said: This one on that day is upon the truth! So I stood up to him, took him by his upper arms, turned his face toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Messenger of Allah, this one? He said: Yes. And behold, it was Uthman ibn Affan."
"17440","360 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ibn Ulayyah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a tribulation and drew it near - then he mentioned the like of it."
"17441","Abu Bakr ibn Bashir from Kab ibn Ujrah. 361 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Umayyah ibn Bistam, narrated to us Mutamir ibn Sulayman, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Jamilah narrate from Abu Bakr ibn Bashir, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When there are rulers over you, whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me nor am I of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin; and whoever enters upon them and does not believe them in their lies nor help them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him. O Kab ibn Ujrah, no flesh nor blood grown from unlawful earnings will enter Paradise; every flesh and blood grown from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more deserving of them. O Kab ibn Ujrah, there are two who go out early and return: one who goes out to ransom his neck and frees it, and one who goes out and destroys it. O Kab ibn Ujrah, prayer is a proof, and fasting is a shield."
"17442","Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Kab ibn Ujrah. 362 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bakr, Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to me, narrated to us Abu Qahdham, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ashath, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was telling us about tribulations, when a man wearing a face-cover passed, so he said: This one on that day and his companions are upon guidance! So I stood up, caught up with him, uncovered the cover from his head, and behold it was Uthman ibn Affan. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this one? He said: Yes."
"17443","Umm Humayd bint Ubayd ibn Rifah from Kab ibn Ujrah. 363 - Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud, narrated to us Abu Dawud, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, Humaydah bint Ubayd narrated to me, from her mother, from Kab ibn Ujrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: I had ascended knowing the Night of Decree, then I was made to forget it, so seek it in the last ten nights, in the odd nights."
"17444","A man of the Ansar from Kab ibn Ujrah. 364 - Narrated to us Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi reported to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from a man of the Ansar, from Kab ibn Ujrah: He suffered harm in his head, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to shave it and to ransom with a cow."
"17445","365 - Narrated to us Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Ibn Abi Fudayk, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, from his father, from a man of the Ansar, from Kab ibn Ujrah: He suffered harm in his head, so he shaved it, and said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): With what should I offer sacrifice? So he ordered him to give a sacrificial animal, garland it, then drive it until he halts with it at Arafah with the people, then move with the people, and likewise he does with the sacrificial animal."
"17446","Kab ibn Amr Abu al-Yasar al-Ansari, then al-Khazraji, Aqabi and Badri. 366 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: Among the names of those who attended al-Aqabah of the Ansar: Abu al-Yasar Kab ibn Amr ibn Abbad, and he attended Badr."
"17447","367 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi, narrated to us Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi, narrated to us Ziyad ibn Abdullah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Among the names of those who attended Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu al-Khazraj: Abu al-Yasar Kab ibn Amr ibn Abbad ibn Amr ibn Ghanm ibn Sawwad ibn Ghanm ibn Kab ibn Salamah ibn Ali."
"17448","368 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, he said: Abu al-Yasar Kab ibn Amr died in the year fifty-five in Madinah, and it is said: He was the last of the people of Badr to die."
"17449","369 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, he said: Abu al-Yasar Kab ibn Amr died in the year fifty-five in Madinah."
"17450","Among what Kab ibn Amr Abu al-Yasar narrated: Ammar ibn Abi al-Yasar from his father. 370 - Narrated to us Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran, Muhammad narrated to me, from Musa, from Umarah ibn Ammar ibn Abi al-Yasar, from his father, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: On the day of Badr I looked at al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib standing as though an idol, his eyes shedding tears; when I looked at him I said: May Allah reward you with evil, O kinsman, do you fight the son of your brother alongside his enemy? He said: What happened to him? Was he killed? I said: Allah is Mightier for him and more Helping than that. He said: What do you want from me? I said: Captivity, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing you. He said: This is not his first kindness. So I took him captive, then brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17451","Musa ibn Talhah from Abu al-Yasar. 371 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi (H). And narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali (H). And narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi - all said: Narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: A woman came to me buying dates from me, so I said: In the house there are dates better than these. She entered the house with me, so I inclined toward her, squeezed her and kissed her, then remorse seized me. So I came to Abu Bakr and mentioned that to him, and he said: Conceal yourself and do not tell anyone. But I could not bear it, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Did you betray a warrior in his family with the like of this? Until I wished I had not become Muslim except at that hour, until I thought I was of the people of the Fire. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed his head in silence for a long time, then Allah revealed to him: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day, to the end of the verse. Abu al-Yasar said: So I came to him and he recited it to me. His Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically or for people generally? He said: Rather, for people generally."
"17452","Ribi ibn Hirash from Abu al-Yasar. 372 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Zaidah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits his debt, Allah will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade."
"17453","Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Abu al-Yasar. 373 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Awn ibn Abdullah, he said: Abu al-Yasar had a debt upon a man, so he came to demand it from him among his family, and he said to his slave-girl: Say: He is not here! But he heard his voice, so he said: Come out, for I have heard your voice! So he came out to him and said: What made you do what you did? He said: Hardship! He said: By Allah? He said: By Allah. He said: Go, for what is upon you is yours - I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits his debt will be in the shade of Allah on the Day of Resurrection, or in the shelter of Allah."
"17454","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn from Abu al-Yasar. 374 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Hatim ibn Ismail, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits his debt, Allah will shade him in the shade of His Throne."
"17455","375 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to be shaded from the blaze of Hell, let him grant respite to a debtor or remit for one in hardship."
"17456","Hanzalah ibn Qays from Abu al-Yasar. 376 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah, from Hanzalah ibn Qays, from Abu al-Yasar al-Badri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves that Allah shade him in His shade, let him grant respite to one in hardship or remit for him."
"17457","Abu Yunus Sulaym ibn Jubayr, freedman of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu al-Yasar. 377 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui al-Qadi, narrated to us Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, Abu Yunus narrated to us that Abu al-Yasar narrated to him, he said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first of people to be shaded in the shade of Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a man who grants respite to one in hardship until he finds something, or gives in charity to him what he seeks from him, saying: What is owed to me from you is charity, seeking the Face of Allah - and he burns his record."
"17458","Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Abu al-Yasar. 378 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Abu Usamah, Thabit ibn Dinar narrated to me, Salim ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yasar al-Ansari said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Amir al-Ashari came to him and said: You sent me for such-and-such, then I came to Mutah. When the ranks were drawn up, Jafar mounted his horse, wore his armor, took the banner and walked until he reached the people, then called out: Who will deliver this to its owner? A man of the people said: I will. So he sent it, then advanced and struck with his sword until he was killed. So the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flowed with tears. Then he led us in Zuhr prayer, then entered and did not speak to us. Then Asr was called, so he came out and prayed, then entered and did not speak to us. He did likewise at Maghrib and Isha, entering and not speaking to us - and when he prayed he used to face us. Then he came out to us at Fajr at the hour he used to come out, while I and Abu Amir al-Ashari were sitting, so he sat between us and said: Shall I not tell you of a dream I saw? I entered Paradise and saw Jafar with two wings stained with blood, and Zayd facing him, and Ibn Rawahah with them as though turning away from them. And I shall tell you about that: When Jafar advanced and saw killing, he did not turn his face away, and Zayd likewise, but Ibn Rawahah turned his face away."
"17459","Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit from Abu al-Yasar. 379 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr (H). And narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah (H). And narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki - all said: Narrated to us Hatim ibn Ismail, from Abu Hazrah Yaqub ibn Mujahid al-Madani, from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: I went out, I and my father, seeking knowledge among this tribe of the Ansar before they perished, and the first whom we met was Abu al-Yasar al-Sulami, Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a slave-boy of his; upon him was a cloak and upon his slave-boy a cloak, a Yemeni garment and a bundle with a copy of the Quran. My father said to him: I see in your face a trace of anger, as it were! He said: Yes; such-and-such son of such-and-such al-Harami owed me money, so I came to his family and said: Is he there? They said: No. Then a sturdy son of his came out to me, so I said to him: Where is your father? He said: He heard your speech and hid in my mother's couch! So I said: Come out to me, for I know where you are! So he came out to me, and I said: What made you hide from me? He said: By Allah, I shall tell you truthfully and not lie to you: By Allah I feared to speak to you and lie to you, or promise you and break my promise, while you were a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and by Allah I was in hardship! He said: By Allah? So I said: By Allah. He said: By Allah? So I said: By Allah. He said: By Allah? So I said: By Allah. Then I forgot the document and erased the debt, and said: If you find means to repay, then repay, otherwise you are absolved. So I bear witness: These two eyes of mine saw - and he placed his fingers upon his eyes - and these two ears of mine heard - and he placed his fingers in his ears - and this heart of mine retained - and he pointed to the place of his heart - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits for him, Allah will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade. I said to him: O uncle, if only you took your slave-boy's cloak and gave him your Yemeni garment, and took his Yemeni garment and gave him your cloak, so that upon you would be a suit and upon him a suit! So he wiped my head and said: O Allah, bless him. O son of my brother, these two eyes of mine saw, these two ears of mine heard, and my heart retained - and he pointed to his eyes, his ears and the place of his heart - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear; and that I should give him of the wealth of this world is dearer to me than that he take of my good deeds on the Day of Resurrection."
"17460","380 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Hanzalah ibn Amr al-Dawraqi, from Abu Hazrah Yaqub ibn Mujahid, from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits for him, Allah will shade him on a day when there is no shade but His shade."
"17461","Sayfi, freedman of Abu Ayyub, from Abu al-Yasar. 381 - Narrated to us Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Anas ibn Iyad (H). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, narrated to us Makki ibn Ibrahim (H). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jafar - all said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, Sayfi, freedman of Abu Ayyub, narrated to us, from Abu al-Yasar al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from being crushed under rubble, and I seek refuge in You from falling, and I seek refuge in You from drowning and burning, and I seek refuge in You from Satan tossing me about at death, and I seek refuge in You from dying of a sting."
"17462","An unnamed man from Abu al-Yasar. 382 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from a man, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will kill Ammar."
"17463","383 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us al-Azraq ibn Ali, narrated to us Hassan ibn Ibrahim, from Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from a man, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will indeed kill Ammar."
"17464","384 - Narrated to us Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from a man, from Abu al-Yasar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared inviolable what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah."
"17465","Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari. 385 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq (H). And narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abu Asim - both from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab narrated to me that Safwan ibn Abdullah narrated to him, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17466","386 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari - and he was of the people of the ship - he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17467","387 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, Mamar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Not of righteousness is fasting while traveling."
"17468","388 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi (H). And narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us al-Qanabi (H). And narrated to us Abu Shuayb al-Harrani, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi (H). And narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah al-Hizami (H). And narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad - all said: Narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17469","389 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Yahya, from al-Layth (H). And narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17470","390 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman (H). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Umar ibn Sulayt - both said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Kathir, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17471","391 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yusuf, narrated to us Yahya ibn Hamzah, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17472","392 - Narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Muafa ibn Sulayman, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Musa ibn Ayan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim: He heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17473","393 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Shair, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abi Hakim, narrated to us Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17474","394 - Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi, narrated to us Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lakhmi, narrated to us Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq, he said: Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17475","395 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Masruq ibn al-Marzuban, narrated to us Marwan ibn Muawiyah, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17476","396 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zanbaqi al-Basri, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17477","397 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Rawh ibn Ubadah, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17478","398 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Walid al-Ghubari, narrated to us Habban ibn Hilal, narrated to us Umarah ibn Zadham, Makhul al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17479","399 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Abbad (H). And narrated to us Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli, narrated to us Salamah ibn Rawh, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Safwan, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari: He heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"17480","Chapter. 400 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ubadah al-Wasiti, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, Karamah bint al-Husayn ibn Jafar ibn al-Harith al-Ansariyyah narrated to me, she said: I heard my father narrate from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) address in the Farewell Pilgrimage in the middle of the days of Tashriq, saying: Is this day inviolable? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then your inviolability among yourselves is like the inviolability of this day of yours. Shall I tell you who the Muslim is? The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. Shall I tell you who the believer is? The one whom the Muslims trust with their lives and wealth. And shall I tell you who the emigrant is? The emigrant is the one who abandons evil deeds from what Allah has forbidden him. And the believer is inviolable to the believer like the inviolability of this day: his flesh is inviolable to him, that he eat it in backbiting and slander him; his honor is inviolable to him, that he tear it; his face is inviolable to him, that he strike it; harming him is inviolable to him, that he harm him; and it is inviolable to him to push him with a push that shakes him."
"17481","401 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Bishr ibn Adam, he said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Karamah bint al-Husayn ibn al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Kab al-Mazini narrated to me - and Abdullah ibn Kab was in charge of the baggage of the Prophet on the day of Badr - she said: I heard my father narrate from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari narrated to me, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) address in the middle of the days of sacrifice at the pillar."
"17482","Kab ibn Zuhayr ibn Abi Sulma al-Muzani. 402 - Narrated to us Abu Khalifah, from Muhammad ibn Sallam, he said: The name of Abu Sulma is Rabiah ibn Riyah ibn Quraz ibn al-Harith ibn Mazin ibn Thalabah ibn Thawr ibn Hadmah ibn Lati ibn Uthman ibn Muzaynah."
"17483","403 - Narrated to us Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Jafar al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah on his return from Taif, Bujayr ibn Zuhayr ibn Abi Sulma wrote to his brother Kab ibn Zuhayr ibn Abi Sulma informing him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had killed a man in Makkah of those who used to satirize him and harm him, and that of the poets of Quraysh who remained, Ibn al-Zibira and Hubayrah ibn Abi Wahb had fled in every direction; so if you care for yourself, flee to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he does not kill anyone who comes repentant, and if you do not, then save yourself. And Kab had composed verses in which he disparaged the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the letter reached Kab, the earth became strait for him, he feared for himself, and those of his enemies who were present spread rumors about him, saying: He will be killed! When he found no alternative, he composed his poem in which he praised the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned his fear and the rumors of the slanderers about him, then went out until he came to Madinah and stayed with a man of Juhaynah between whom and him there was acquaintance, as was mentioned to me. He went with him in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he had prayed Fajr, so he prayed with the people, then pointed out the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to him and said: This is the Messenger of Allah, so stand up to him and seek his protection! It was mentioned to me that he stood up to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he placed his hand in his hand, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not know him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Kab ibn Zuhayr has come seeking protection from you, repentant and Muslim - will you accept him if I bring him to you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am Kab ibn Zuhayr! Ibn Ishaq said: Asim ibn Amr ibn Qatadah narrated to me, he said: A man of the Ansar leapt upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, leave me with the enemy of Allah that I may strike his neck! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for he has come repentant and turning back! So he became angry at this tribe of the Ansar because of what their companion did to him, since no man of the Emigrants spoke of him except with good, and he recited his poem which he composed when he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Ishaq said: Asim ibn Amr narrated to me, he said: When he said the words about the dark tall ones - intending thereby the Ansar - because of what their companion had done, and singled out the Emigrants of Quraysh among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his praise, the Ansar became angry with him. Then after he became Muslim he composed praising the Ansar and mentioning their valor with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and their station with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17484","Kab ibn Iyad al-Ashari. 404 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him, from his father, from Kab ibn Iyad, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every nation has a trial, and the trial of my nation is wealth."
"17485","405 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yahya al-Iskandarani, narrated to us Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Kab ibn Iyad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Storytellers are three: a ruler, or one commanded, or one boastful."
"17486","406 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi, narrated to us al-Musayyab ibn Wadih, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Layth ibn Sad, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Kab ibn Iyad al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If the son of Adam were given two valleys of wealth, he would wish a third to them, and nothing fills the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"17487","Kab ibn Amr al-Yami. 407 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Mamar al-Muqad, narrated to us Abd al-Warith ibn Said, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe his head once like this, until he reached the nape."
"17488","408 - Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abd al-Warith, from Layth, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe his head from its front to its back, bringing his hands out from beneath his ears."
"17489","409 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated to us Abu Salamah al-Kindi, narrated to us Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, rinsing his mouth three times and sniffing water three times, taking fresh water for each, and washed his face three times; when he wiped his head he did like this - and he gestured with his hand from the front of his head until he brought them to the bottom of his neck from the side of his nape."
"17490","410 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Umayyah ibn Bistam, narrated to us Mutamir, narrated to us Layth, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution, water flowing from his face onto his beard and chest; he separated between rinsing the mouth and sniffing."
"17491","411 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Said ibn Anbasah al-Khazzaz, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Harb, narrated to us Malik ibn Mighwal, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe his head."
"17492","412 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami, my father Musarrif ibn Amr ibn al-Sari ibn Musarrif ibn Kab ibn Amr narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, reaching Kab ibn Amr, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe the inside of his beard and his nape."
"17493","Kab ibn Qutbah. 413 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari."
"17494","Those named Kulthum: Kulthum ibn Husayn Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari, and he is Kulthum ibn Husayn ibn Ubayd ibn Khalaf ibn Qays ibn Ahmas ibn Affan ibn Muqbil ibn Damrah ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Kinanah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar ibn Nizar ibn Madd ibn Adnan, and he was of those who pledged under the tree. 414 - Narrated to us Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Jafar al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for the conquest of Makkah, he left Abu Ruhm Kulthum ibn al-Husayn al-Ghifari in charge of Madinah."
"17495","What Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari narrated. 415 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, the son of the brother of Abu Ruhm informed me that he heard Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari - and he was of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who pledged under the tree - say: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Tabuk. When we traveled by night, I rode close to him, then drowsiness overcame me, and I would wake with my mount drawn near his mount, and its nearness would startle me lest I strike his foot in the stirrup, so I would hold my mount back, until sleep overcame my eyes in part of the night and my mount jostled his foot in the stirrup and struck his foot. I woke only at his saying: Hiss! I said: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah! He said: Go on. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began asking about those of Banu Ghifar who stayed behind, and I informed him, and as he asked me: What happened to the red, tall, thin ones? I told him of their staying behind. He said: What happened to the black - or he said: the short, curly-haired, thin - group who own camels at Shabakah Sarah? He said: I recalled Banu Ghifar but could not remember them, until I remembered a clan of Aslam, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, they are a clan of Aslam who stayed behind! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevents one of those, when he stays behind, from mounting an energetic man in the path of Allah upon a camel of his camels? For the dearest of my family to me are that the Emigrants of Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam and Ghifar should not stay behind from me."
"17496","416 - Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, the son of the brother of Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari narrated to me that he heard Abu Ruhm - and he was of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who pledged under the tree - say: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one night I rode close to him. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"17497","417 - Abu Usamah al-Halabi narrated to me, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi, my grandfather narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, the son of the brother of Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari informed me that he heard Abu Ruhm - and he was of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who pledged under the tree - say: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of Tabuk, and when he returned he traveled by night at al-Akhdar. I rode close to him, and drowsiness was cast upon us, and I would wake with my mount drawn near his mount, and its nearness would startle me, until I feared I would strike his foot in the stirrup, so I would hold my mount back, until my eyes overcame me in part of the night and my mount jostled the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the stirrup and struck his foot. I woke only at his saying: Hiss! I said: O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me! He said: Go on. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began asking me about those of Banu Ghifar who stayed behind, and I informed him. He said as he asked me: What happened to the red, tall, thin group? I told him of their staying behind. He said: What happened to the black, locust-like, short group who own camels at Shabakah Sarah? He said: I recalled Banu Ghifar but could not remember them, until I remembered that they were a clan of Aslam who stayed behind. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevents one of those, when he stays behind, from mounting an energetic man in the path of Allah upon a camel of his camels? For the dearest of my family to me are that the Emigrants of Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam and Ghifar should not stay behind from me. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated it from al-Zuhri, with Ibn Ukaymah between him and the son of the brother of Abu Ruhm."
"17498","418 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi, narrated to us Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi, narrated to us Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukaymah al-Laythi, from the son of the brother of Abu Ruhm, that he heard Abu Ruhm Kulthum ibn Husayn, of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who pledged under the tree, say: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of Tabuk, and one night I rode with him while we were at al-Akhdar, close to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and drowsiness was cast upon us, and I would wake with my mount drawn near the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and its nearness would startle me lest I strike his foot in the stirrup, so I would steer my mount away from him, until my eyes overcame me on part of the road in part of the night, and my mount jostled the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his foot was in the stirrup. I woke only at his saying: Hiss! I said: O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me! He said: Go on. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began asking me about those of Banu Ghifar who stayed behind, and I informed him of them. He said as he asked me: What happened to the red, tall, thin group? I told him of their staying behind. He said: What happened to the black, curly-haired, short ones? He said: I said: By Allah, I do not know them among us! He said: Yes, those who own camels at Shabakah Shadkh? So I recalled them among Banu Ghifar but could not remember them, until I remembered that they were a clan of Aslam who were allies among us, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, they are a clan of Aslam who were allies among us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevents one of those, when he stays behind, from mounting an energetic man in the path of Allah upon a camel of his camels? The dearest of my family to me are that the Emigrants of Quraysh, the Ansar, Ghifar and Aslam should not stay behind from me."
"17499","419 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali (H). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Dabbi - both said: Narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sulami, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah al-Madani, from Abu Hazim, freedman of Abu Ruhm, my master Abu Ruhm narrated to me, he said: I and my brother attended Khaybar with two horses, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted us six shares: four shares for the two horses, and two shares for us. So we sold our two shares for two young camels."
"17500","420 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, from Abu Hazim, freedman of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Ruhm and from his brother: They were two horsemen on the day of Khaybar, so they were given six shares: four for their two horses and two shares for them. So they sold the two shares for two young camels."
"17501","Kaladah ibn Hanbal al-Ghassani, ally of Banu Jumah, who used to reside in Makkah, and he is Kaladah ibn Hanbal ibn Malik ibn Aidah ibn Kilwah, his mother Unaysah bint Mamar ibn Habib ibn Wahb ibn Hudhafah ibn Jumah, and he is the maternal brother of Safwan ibn Umayyah; his father allied with Mamar and married him his daughter. What Kaladah ibn Hanbal narrated. 421 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Misri al-Ubulli, narrated to us Abu Asim (H). And narrated to us Abu Khalifah, narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj al-Riyashi (H). And narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah al-Sayrafi al-Basri, narrated to us Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali - both said: Narrated to us Abu Asim (H). And narrated to us Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar, narrated to us Rawh ibn Ubadah (H). And narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Rawh ibn Ubadah - both said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Sufyan informed me that Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan informed him that Kaladah ibn Hanbal informed him: Safwan ibn Umayyah sent him at the conquest to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with milk, a young goat and daghabis, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the upper part of the valley. So I entered without seeking permission and without greeting, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go out and say: Peace be upon you, may I enter? And that was after Safwan had become Muslim. Abu Asim said: Daghabis is a herb found in the desert."
"17502","Those named Kudayr: Kudayr al-Dabbi, who used to reside in Kufah, and his Companionship is disputed. 422 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, Kudayr al-Dabbi informed me: A Bedouin man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Tell me of a deed that brings me near Paradise and distances me from Hellfire! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are these two what concern you? He said: Yes. He said: Speak justly, and give of surplus. He said: By Allah, I cannot speak justly every hour, nor can I give of the surplus of my wealth. He said: Feed food, and spread peace. He said: This too is hard. He said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: Look to a camel of your camels and a water-skin, then head to a household who drink water only every other day and give them to drink; perhaps your camel will not perish nor your water-skin tear before Paradise becomes due for you. So the Bedouin went off uttering takbir, and his water-skin did not tear nor his camel perish before he was killed as a martyr."
"17503","Those named Kathir: Kathir ibn al-Abbas. 423 - Narrated to us Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Harithi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Anbasah, narrated to us Ali ibn Hashim, from al-Sabbah ibn Yahya, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Abbas ibn Kathir, from Kathir ibn al-Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gather us - me, Abdullah, Ubaydullah and Qutham - spreading his arms like this, extending his reach, and saying: Whoever races to me first, for him is such-and-such."
"17504","Those named Kurayz: Kurayz ibn Samah. 424 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah and Ahmad ibn Mabihram al-Idhaji - both said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati, narrated to us Yahya ibn Rashid, narrated to us al-Rahhal ibn al-Mundhir ibn Yazid al-Umari, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Kurayz ibn Samah - and he had come as a delegate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, invoke against Banu Amir! He said: I was not sent as one who curses."
"17505","425 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar, narrated to us Amr ibn Busr, narrated to us Yahya ibn Rashid, narrated to us al-Rahhal ibn al-Mundhir, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Kurayz ibn Samah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tied a red banner for Banu Sulaym."
"17506","Those named Kardam: Kardam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, Abu Maymunah. 426 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Kab al-Taifi - from Yazid ibn Miqsam, from Maymunah bint Kardam: She was riding behind her father and heard her father ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I have vowed to slaughter at Buwanah! He said: Is there an idol there or a false deity worshipped? He said: No. He said: Fulfill your vow."
"17507","427 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr: Kardam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have vowed to slaughter a herd of camels at Buwanah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: For an idol? He said: No. He said: For a gathering of the gatherings of ignorance? He said: No. He said: Fulfill your vow wherever it is. O Kardam, there is no vow nor oath in disobedience to Allah."
"17508","428 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Thaqafi, he said: Sarah bint Miqsam narrated to me, from Maymunah daughter of Kardam, from her father Kardam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi: A man said: O Messenger of Allah! So he inclined toward him and said: Where is the year of the army of Ithran? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recognized that army - I was in that army - and Tariq ibn al-Muraqqi said: Who will give me a spear for its reward? I said: What is its reward? He said: The first daughter born to me, I shall marry her to him. So I gave him my spear, and it deflected something from him. Then it reached me that a daughter was born to him and she had grown up, so I said: Hand over my family to me. But he refused except with a dowry. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And of what worth among women is she? He said: She has seen old age. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is better for you neither to sin nor cause sin; leave her alone."
"17509","Kardam ibn Qays. 429 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Hawti, both said: Narrated to us Abu al-Yaman, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from Ibrahim ibn Amr, he said: I heard Kardam ibn Qays say: I went out, I and a cousin of mine called Abu Thalabah, on a hot day, wearing sandals while he had none. He said: Give me your sandal. I said: No, unless you marry me your daughter. He said: Give it, for I have married her to you. When we returned, he sent me my sandals and said: You have no wife with me. So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Leave her, there is no good in her for you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have vowed to slaughter a herd of camels of my herd at such-and-such place! He said: Fulfill your vow; there is no vow in severing kinship nor in what the son of Adam does not own."
"17510","Kardam ibn Abi al-Saib. 430 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Kufi, narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Kardam ibn Abi al-Saib, he said: I went out with my father from Madinah intending Makkah for a need, and that was when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was first mentioned in Makkah. He brought us to a shepherd, and at midnight a wolf came and took a lamb of his sheep. The shepherd leapt up and said: O Amir of the valley, your neighbor! He said: We heard a voice whose speaker we did not see: O Sarhan, release it! He said: The lamb came running with no bite upon it until it entered among the sheep. He said: And it was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Madinah: And there were men of mankind who sought refuge with men of the jinn, the verse."
"17511","Remainder of the chapter of Kaf: Those named Kannaz: Kannaz ibn Husayn, Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi. 431 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Sudai, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu Marthad Kannaz ibn Husayn ibn Yarbu ibn Amrah ibn Yarbu ibn Kharashah ibn Sad ibn Tarif ibn Jillan - and it is said: Hillan - ibn Ghani ibn Yasar ibn Sad ibn Qays Ghaylan ibn Mudar."
"17512","432 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: Among the names of those who attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, ally of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. Abu Marthad died in the year twelve, at the age of sixty-six."
"17513","433 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim (H). And narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yusuf (H). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar - both said: Sadqah ibn Khalid narrated to us - both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa say: I heard Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not sit upon graves nor pray toward them."
"17514","434 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to me, narrated to us Nuaym ibn Hammad (H). And narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi - both said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: I heard Busr ibn Ubaydullah narrate from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, from Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not sit toward graves nor pray toward them."
"17515","Those named Kahmas: Kahmas al-Hilali. 435 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Musa ibn Ismail, narrated to us Hammad ibn Yazid al-Minqari, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Kahmas al-Hilali, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stayed with him, then left him, then came to him after a year and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not recognize me? He said: No. I said: I am the one who was with you last year! He said: What changed you after me? He said: I have not eaten food in daytime since I left you! He said: Who ordered you to torment yourself? Fast a day of the lunar days. I said: Give me more! So he gave me more, until he said: Fast three days of the month."
"17516","Those named Kaysan: Kaysan Abu Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Salamah ibn Usayd. 436 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Abu Awn al-Ziyadi, narrated to us Amr ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kaysan, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come out of the kitchens until he came to the well of prayer, wrapped in a waist-wrapper, and prayed two rakahs of Zuhr or Asr, crossing its two ends."
"17517","437 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafii, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hanzalah, from Maruf ibn Mushkan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kaysan, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray at the upper well in a single garment."
"17518","Kaysan, Abu Nafi, also given the kunyah Abu Rafi. 438 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Yahya, Ibn Lahiah reported to us, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nafi ibn Kaysan al-Dimashqi: His father Kaysan himself informed him that he used to trade in wine in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he came from Syria with wine in skins intending trade, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have brought a fine drink! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Kaysan, it has been forbidden! Kaysan said: Shall I go and sell it, O Prophet of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been forbidden, and its price is forbidden! So Kaysan went to the skins, seized them by their legs, then poured them all out."
"17519","439 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Abu Hatim al-Razi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan, my father Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid al-Fadaki informed me, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Taifi informed me that Nafi ibn Kaysan informed him that his father carried wine to Madinah before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it; he came to him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What have you brought, O Abu Rafi? He said: Wine, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not know that it has been forbidden after you? He said: Shall I sell it to the Jews? He said: Its seller is like its drinker! So Abu Rafi tore open his skins at al-Batha."
"17520","440 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Hisham ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to us Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Nafi ibn Kaysan, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Jesus son of Mary, upon him be peace, will descend at the white minaret in Damascus."
"17521","Those named Kadan: Kadan ibn Abd al-Akki. 441 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ramli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fihr ibn Jamil ibn Abi Karīm al-Akki of Yafa, Umayyah and Lifaf, sons of al-Mufaddal ibn Abi Karīm ibn Lifaf ibn Kadan, narrated to me, from their father, from their grandfather, from Lifaf ibn Kadan, from his father Kadan ibn Abd, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Yemen, pledged to him, and became Muslim at his hands."
"17522","Those named Kurz: Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Khuzai, who used to reside in Madinah. 442 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Khuzai, he said: A Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, does Islam have an end? He said: Yes; whatever household of Arabs or non-Arabs Allah intends good for, He brings Islam into them. He said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then tribulations occur like the night. He said: The Bedouin said: By no means, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By no means; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, black masses will be led therein, some of you striking the necks of others."
"17523","443 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi (H). And narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah (H). And narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi - all said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Kurz ibn Alqamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17524","444 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr: Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Khuzai said: While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of the Bedouins came and said: O Messenger of Allah, does Islam have an end? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; whatever household of Arabs or non-Arabs Allah intends good for, He brings Islam into them. The Bedouin said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then tribulations occur like shades. The Bedouin said: By no means, O Messenger of Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will return therein as black masses, some of you striking the necks of others."
"17525","445 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn Yahya narrated to me, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Khuzai said: While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of the Bedouins of Najd came, saying: O Messenger of Allah, does Islam have an end? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; whatever household of Arabs or non-Arabs Allah intends good for, He brings Islam into them. The Bedouin said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then tribulations occur like shades. The Bedouin said: By no means, O Messenger of Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will return therein as black masses, some of you striking the necks of others."
"17526","446 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah ibn Yahya, my grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to me, Idris ibn Yahya al-Khawlani narrated to me, narrated to us Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Kurz, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - then he mentioned the like of it."
"17527","Kurz ibn Jabir al-Qurashi, then al-Fihri; he was martyred with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest. 447 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: Among the names of those martyred on the day of the conquest among the Muslims, of Quraysh, then of Banu Muharib ibn Fihr: Kurz ibn Jabir."
"17528","Those named Kulayb: Kulayb ibn Shihab ibn Mahbub al-Jarmi, Abu Asim. 448 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri, narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Wahb al-Kufi, Qutbah ibn al-Ala al-Ghanawi narrated to us, my father al-Ala ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi, from his father: He went out with his father to a funeral attended by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and I was a boy who understood - and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves for the worker, when he works, to do it well."
"17529","Kulayb ibn Hazn. 449 - Narrated to us Salamah ibn Nahid al-Maqdisi, narrated to us Ismail ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi, narrated to us Yala ibn al-Ashdaq, from Kulayb ibn Hazn, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, seek Paradise with your utmost effort, and flee from Hellfire with your utmost effort, for the seeker of Paradise does not sleep, and the fleer from Hellfire does not sleep. Verily the Hereafter today is surrounded by hardships, and this world is surrounded by desires."
"17530","Kulayb al-Juhani. 450 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Munib, from Ghunaym ibn Kathir ibn Kulayb al-Juhani, from his father, from his grandfather - and he had Companionship - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eldest of brothers is in the station of the father."
"17531","Chapter of Lam: Those named Laqit: Laqit ibn al-Rabi ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf, Abu al-As, son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); his name is disputed: it is said Mihsham, and it is said al-Qasim. 451 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai, narrated to us al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar, he said: Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi, husband of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and son of her maternal aunt; his mother Halah bint Khuwaylid ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy, sister of Khadijah bint Khuwaylid by her father, and her mother Fatimah bint Zaidah, and he is al-Asamm ibn Jundub ibn Harim ibn Rawahah ibn Hujr ibn Abd ibn Muis ibn Amir ibn Luayy. And it is said the name of Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi is Mihsham, and he was called the Pup of al-Batha. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan and Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to me, both said: The name of Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi is Laqit. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad ibn al-Dahhak narrated to me, from his father, he said: The name of Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi is al-Qasim, and that is the established view of his name. And Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi died in Dhu al-Hijjah of the year twelve."
"17532","452 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi: Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), became Muslim while her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi was a polytheist, then he became Muslim after that after a while, and he did not renew the marriage. Abd al-Razzaq said: And Mamar mentioned, from Jabir, from al-Shabi."
"17533","453 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, Ibn Jurayj reported to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Hasan ibn Muhammad informed him: Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf had married the daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the ransom; Zaynab came to him. Amr said: I do not think but that they were left upon their marriage of the pre-Islamic period."
"17534","454 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Zaynab, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), became Muslim while her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi was a polytheist, then he became Muslim after that, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left them upon their marriage."
"17535","455 - Narrated to us Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Jafar al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Zaynab to Abu al-As with the first marriage and did not introduce anything new. And it is disputed about that, and they said: With a new marriage."
"17536","456 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Humayd, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: Zaynab, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), became Muslim a year before her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi, then he became Muslim, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned her with a new marriage."
"17537","Laqit ibn Amir, Abu Razin al-Uqayli: Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi from Abu Razin. 457 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi (H). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatarani, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb - all said: Shuabah narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Salim, from Amr ibn Aws, from Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who cannot perform Hajj nor Umrah nor travel! He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father, and Umrah - and the wording is of the hadith of Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"17538","458 - Narrated to us Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Shuabah ibn al-Hajjaj, from al-Numan ibn Salim, from Amr ibn Aws, from Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man who cannot perform Hajj nor Umrah nor travel! He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father, and Umrah."
"17539","Waki ibn Hudus - also said Udus - from Abu Razin. 459 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Nusayr, narrated to us Shuabah, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Waki ibn Udus narrate from his uncle Abu Razin al-Uqayli: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the believer is like the bee; it eats only what is pure, and leaves only what is pure."
"17540","460 - Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi, narrated to us Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf al-Jubari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Adi, from Shuabah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus narrating from Abu Razin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the believer is like the bee; he eats only what is pure, and leaves only what is pure."
"17541","461 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Jad, Shuabah and Hushaym reported to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from his uncle Abu Razin al-Uqayli, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dream is a part of forty - or forty-six - parts of prophethood, and it is upon the leg of a bird; when it is interpreted, it occurs. Shuabah said in his hadith: And I think he said: Let him narrate it only to a loving one or one of sound judgment."
"17542","462 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ghundar, from Shuabah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from his uncle Abu Razin: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty parts of prophethood, and it is upon the leg of a bird so long as it is not spoken of; when it is spoken of, it occurs."
"17543","463 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Hudus, from his uncle Abu Razin al-Uqayli: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dream is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood, and a dream hangs upon the leg of a bird until its owner speaks of it; when he speaks of it, it occurs. So let him speak of it only to one who knows, or an adviser, or a beloved."
"17544","464 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Hushaym, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus al-Uqayli, from his uncle Abu Razin al-Uqayli: He heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A dream is upon the leg of a bird so long as it is not interpreted; when it is interpreted, it occurs. And he said: A dream is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood, and I think he said: Let him narrate it only to a loving one or one of sound judgment."
"17545","465 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid (H). And narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Hudus, from Abu Razin, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, will each of us see his Lord on the Day of Resurrection? And what is the sign of that in His creation? He said: Does not each of you see the moon with its light unveiled? I said: Yes. He said: Then Allah is Greater."
"17546","466 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi the judge narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated - both from Shubah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from Abu Razin al-Uqayli, he said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, will all of us see our Lord? He said: Yes. I said: And what is the sign of that in His creation? He said: Does not every one of you look at the moon on the night of the full moon? And it is only a creation from among the creation of Allah, and Allah is greater and more majestic."
"17547","467 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Hudus, from his uncle Abu Razin - and he is Laqit ibn Amir - that he said: We used to slaughter sacrifices in Rajab, eating from them and feeding others, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm in that. And Waki said: I will never abandon it."
"17548","468 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated. And al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated - both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Hudus, from his uncle Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where was our Lord before He created the heaven and the earth? He said: He was in a cloud with no air beneath it and no air above it, then He created His Throne upon the water."
"17549","469 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Hudus, from Abu Razin, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Exalted, laughs at the despair of His servants and the nearness of His relief. Abu Razin said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, does the Lord laugh? He said: Yes. He said: We will never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs."
"17550","470 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated - both said: Ghundar narrated, from Shubah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from his uncle Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah give life to the dead? He said: Have you not passed by the valley of your people when it was barren, then passed by it when it was green, then passed by it when it was barren, then passed by it when it was green? Likewise Allah gives life to the dead."
"17551","471 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated - both said: Ghundar narrated, from Shubah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where is my mother? He said: Your mother is in the Fire. He said: Then where are those of your family who passed away? He said: Are you not pleased that your mother should be with my mother?"
"17552","472 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from his uncle Abu Razin, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike excessive questioning and criticize it, but when Abu Razin asked him, he would answer him, and that pleased him."
"17553","473 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated. And Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated. And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated - they said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri, from his father, he said: I came to Kufah with a companion of mine to bring sandals from there. We went early to the market and it had not yet opened, so I said to my companion: If only we entered the mosque - and the mosque at that time was among the date-sellers - so we entered, and there was a man from Qays called Ibn al-Muntafiq. I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was described to me and made clear to me, so I sought him in Makkah and was told he is in Mina, and I sought him in Mina and was told he is in Arafat. So I reached him while he was among a group of his Companions. It was said to me: Step aside from the path of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the man; does he have some need? So I drew near until I took hold of the reins of his she-camel or its bridle, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I ask you about what will save me from the Fire and what will bring me to Paradise. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to the sky, then lowered it, then turned to me with his face and said: Though you have made your question brief, you have asked about a great and weighty matter, so retain from me: Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, fast Ramadan, and whatever you love that people do to you, do it to them, and whatever you dislike that people do to you, leave people free of it. Let go of the she-camel's rein. Hammam said: As for Hajj, he had already performed Hajj when he asked him."
"17554","474 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh ibn Muadh al-Askari narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Awn narrated, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from a colleague of his reporting from his father - and he was known as Abu al-Muntafiq - he said: I came to Makkah and asked about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: At Arafah. So I came to him and tried to draw near him until the neck of my mount crossed the neck of his mount. I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me what will save me from the punishment of Allah and admit me into His Paradise. He said: Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, perform Hajj and Umrah - and I think he said: And fast Ramadan - and consider what you love for people to do toward you, do it to them, and what you dislike them doing toward you, leave them free of it. Ibn Awn was inconsistent in the isnad of this hadith and did not establish it precisely from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, while Hammam established it precisely."
"17555","475 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated, Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayr narrated, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah, from his father, he said: I reached Ibn al-Muntafiq - and he mentioned it."
"17556","476 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Yahya ibn Isa narrated, from al-Amash, from Umar ibn Murrah, from al-Mughirah ibn Said al-Akhram, from his father or from his uncle - al-Amash doubts - he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting to ask him. Then he mentioned something similar."
"17557","477 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri and Abd Allah ibn al-Saqr al-Askari narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Hizam narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash al-Ansari then al-Mismai narrated to me, from Dalham ibn al-Aswad, from Asim ibn Laqit, that Laqit ibn Amir went as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), accompanied by a companion of his called Nahik ibn Asim ibn Malik ibn al-Muntafiq. Laqit said: I and my companion set out until we arrived at Madinah at the end of Rajab. We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he had finished the dawn prayer. He stood among the people delivering a sermon and said: O people, I have held back my voice for you for four days so that I may make you hear today. Is there any man whom his people sent, saying: Learn for us what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says? Then perhaps his own thoughts distract him, or the talk of his companion distracts him, or the misguided distract him. I am to be asked: Did I convey? So listen and you shall live; listen and you shall live; sit down! He said: So the people sat, and I and my companion stood, until his heart and his sight were free for us. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you have of the knowledge of the unseen? By Allah, he laughed and shook his head, knowing that I sought his slip, and said: Your Lord has withheld five matters of the unseen which none knows but He - and he gestured with his hand. I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Knowledge of death - when the death of any of you will be, and you do not know it; knowledge of the semen when it is in the womb - He has known it and you do not know it; knowledge of what is in tomorrow - He has known what you will eat tomorrow and you do not know it; knowledge of the day of rain - He looks upon you in distress and anxiety, and your Lord continues to laugh, knowing that your relief is near - Laqit said: I said: We will never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs - and knowledge of the Day of the Hour. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I will ask you about my need, so do not hurry me. He said: Ask whatever you wish. I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach us what you teach people and what we know, for we are from a tribe whose attestation is not believed by anyone - neither Madhhij, who are above us, nor Khatham, who are our equals and allies, nor our own clan from which we come. He said: You shall remain as you remain, then the Cry will be sent. By your God, it will leave nothing upon its back but it will die, along with the angels who are with your Lord. Your Lord will come to roam over the earth while the lands are empty of Him. Your Lord will send the sky with rain from near the Throne. By your God, it will leave no slain one upon its back nor any buried dead but the grave will split open from him, and He will create him from the side of his head so that he sits upright. Your Lord will say: What is the matter with you? - for what he was in - he will say: My Lord, yesterday is today - from his recent acquaintance with life, thinking it was just now. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how will He gather us after the winds and decay and beasts of prey have torn us apart? He said: I inform you of the like of that among the blessings of Allah: the earth - you looked upon it when it was a worn-out clod, and you said it would never live; then your Lord sent the sky upon it, and it did not remain upon it but a short while until you looked upon it and it was a single drink of water. By your God, He is more able to gather you from water than to gather the vegetation of the earth. So you will come out from the graves and from the places where you fell, and you will look at Him for a while and He will look at you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how, when we fill the earth and He is a single person looking at us while we look at Him? He said: I inform you of the like of that among the blessings of Allah: the sun and the moon are a small sign of Him - you see them both in a single hour and they both see you, and you suffer no crowding in seeing them both. By your God, He is more able to see you and for you to see Him than for you to see them both and for them both to see you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what will our Lord do with us when we meet Him? He said: You will be presented to Him with your pages open, and nothing hidden of you will be hidden from Him. Your Lord will take a handful of water in His hand and sprinkle your hearts with it. By your God, not a single drop will miss the face of any one of you. As for the Muslim, it will leave his face like white fine cloth, and as for the disbeliever, it will make it like black char. Then He will turn away from you, and the righteous will disperse in His tracks and traverse a bridge over the Fire; one of you will step on a live coal and say: Ah! Then your Lord will say: Its time has come. Then they will look upon the Pond of the Messenger, whose people will never thirst, by Allah. By your God, not one of you will stretch out his hand but a cup will fall upon it, cleansing him of sweat and urine and filth. The sun and the moon will be withheld so you will see neither of them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by what shall we see? He said: By the like of your sight at this hour of yours - and that is with the rising of the sun on a day when the earth is bright and the mountains face it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by what shall we be recompensed for our evil deeds and our good deeds? He said: The good deed is ten times its like, and the evil deed is the like of it, or He forgives. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are Paradise and the Fire? He said: By your God, the Fire has seven gates, and there is no gate among them but a rider travels between them for seventy years; and Paradise has eight gates, and there are no two gates among them but a rider travels between them for seventy years. I said: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall we look out from Paradise? He said: Upon rivers of purified honey, and rivers of a cup free of headache and regret, and rivers of milk whose taste has not changed, and water that is not stagnant, and fruits - by your God - such as you know, and good of the like thereof along with it, and purified spouses. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we have wives in it, and are any of them righteous? He said: Righteous women are for righteous men; you will enjoy them as you enjoyed in this world, and they will enjoy you, except that there will be no offspring. Laqit said: I said: What is the best thing we can attain and reach? I said: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall I pledge allegiance to you? He extended his hand and said: Upon establishing prayer, giving zakah, and abandoning polytheism - do not associate with Allah any other god. He said: I said to him: And what is between the east and the west? He clasped and opened his fingers, thinking that I was stipulating something he would not grant me. He said: I said: We may settle from it wherever we wish, and no soul earns but against itself. He extended his hand and said: Then it is yours; settle wherever you wish, and none shall earn against you but your own soul. He said: So we turned away from him, and he said: Lo, these two - lo, these two - are from a group; by your God, they are among the people most fearful of their Lord in this world and the Hereafter. Kab ibn al-Khudariyyah, one of Banu Abi Bakr ibn Kilab, said to him: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Banu al-Muntafiq. He said: Banu al-Muntafiq are worthy of that; they are worthy of that. So I turned away and came back to him, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any good for anyone who passed away before us in their ignorance? A man from the Quraysh crowd said: By Allah, your father al-Muntafiq is in the Fire. He said: It was as if heat fell between the skin of my face and its flesh because of what he said in front of the people, and I intended to say: Where is your father, O Messenger of Allah? But the other course was better, so I said: And your family, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And my family. Whatever grave of an Amiri or a Qurashi polytheist you pass, say: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has sent me to you, so receive glad tidings of what displeases you: you will be dragged upon your face and your belly in the Fire. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what did that to them, when they were upon a practice they knew nothing good but it, and they thought they were righteous? He said: That is because Allah sent at the end of every seven nations a prophet; whoever obeyed his prophet was among the guided, and whoever disobeyed him was among the misguided."
"17558","478 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Razin, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning game that disappears from its hunter: He said: Perhaps the vermin of the earth killed it."
"17559","Laqit ibn Sabirah al-Uqayli. 479 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ismail ibn Kathir informed me, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father, he said: I and a companion of mine set out until we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but we did not find him. Aishah fed us dates and cooked porridge for us, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking briskly. He said: Did you feed them anything? We said: Yes. While we were upon that, the shepherd drove the sheep to the fold with a kid in his hand. He said: Has it given birth? He said: Yes. He said: Then slaughter a sheep. Then he turned to us with his face and said: Do not think - and he did not say: Do not ever think - that we slaughtered the sheep on your account. We have one hundred sheep and we do not want them to increase beyond that; whenever a lamb is born to the shepherd, we command him and he slaughters a sheep. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about ablution. He said: When you perform ablution, perform it fully and run the fingers between one another, and when you blow your nose, do so thoroughly, unless you are fasting. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife - and he mentioned her long tongue and foul speech. He said: Divorce her. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, she has long companionship and children! He said: Keep her and command her; if there is good in her, she will do it. And do not beat your wife as you beat your slave-girl."
"17560","480 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Taifi narrated, from Ismail ibn Kathir, from Asim ibn Laqit, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17561","481 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ismail ibn Kathir, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned something, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution fully, and run the fingers between one another."
"17562","482 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated - both said: Sufyan narrated, from Abu Hashim, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Perform ablution fully, run the fingers between one another, and when you sniff water into the nose, do so thoroughly, unless you are fasting - and their wording is one."
"17563","483 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Hassan al-Attar al-Basri narrated, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated, from Ismail ibn Kathir, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father - the delegate of Banu al-Muntafiq - that he came to Aishah, he and a companion of his, seeking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but they did not find him. Aishah fed them porridge. It was not long before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking briskly, swaying. He said: Did you feed them? We said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, about prayer? He said: Perform ablution fully, run the fingers between one another, and be thorough in sniffing water into the nose, unless you are fasting. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife - and he mentioned her affliction. He said: Divorce her. I said: She has long companionship and children! He said: Then admonish her; if there is good in her, she will do it. And do not beat your wife as you beat your slave-girl. While we were like that, the shepherd of the sheep drove them, with a kid in his hands in the fold. He said: Has it given birth? He said: Yes. He said: A lamb - he said - slaughter a sheep in its place. Then he turned to me and said: Do not think - and he did not say: Do not ever think - that we slaughtered it on your account. We have one hundred sheep and we do not wish them to increase beyond that; whenever the shepherd's ewe gives birth to a lamb, we command him and he slaughters a sheep."
"17564","Laqit ibn Artatah al-Sakuni. 484 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated, Nasr ibn Alqamah narrated, from his brother, from Ibn Aidh, from Laqit ibn Artatah al-Sakuni, that a man said to him: We have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits indecency, so report his case to the ruler! He said: I killed ninety-nine alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I would not love to have killed the like of them and to have uncovered the veil of a Muslim."
"17565","485 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu Alqamah Nasr ibn Khuzaymah narrated, that his father narrated to him, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother Mahfuz ibn Alqamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh, he said: Laqit ibn Sabirah al-Sakuni said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while my feet were crooked and did not touch the ground, so he supplicated for me and I walked upon the ground."
"17566","Those named Lubayy. Lubayy ibn Labba. 486 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated, from Abu Balj, he said: I saw Lubayy ibn Labba al-Asadi - and he was a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a horse of his outran, so he covered it with an Adani cloak, and I saw upon him a garment of silk brocade or a bordered cloak."
"17567","Those named Lajlaj. Lajlaj Abu Khalid, who used to reside in Damascus. 487 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, al-Mualla ibn al-Walid al-Qaqaai narrated, Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ala ibn al-Lajlaj narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather al-Lajlaj, he said: I have not filled my belly with food since I accepted Islam with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I eat what suffices me and I drink what suffices me. Al-Ala said: Meaning his sustenance."
"17568","488 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs al-Ataki narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar narrated, from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj, who narrated to him that his father al-Lajlaj informed him that he was sitting in the market when a woman carrying a boy passed by. The people rushed and I rushed. We proceeded until we reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was saying: Who is the father of this one with you? She fell silent. A youth beside her said: I am his father, O Messenger of Allah! He turned to her and said: Who is the father of this one with you? She fell silent. The young man said: O Messenger of Allah, she is young in age, recently defiled, and she will not speak to you; I am his father, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at some of his Companions as if asking them about him. They said: We know nothing but good, or something like that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you married? He said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he be stoned. We went out with him and dug for him until we secured him, then we pelted him with stones until he became still. Then we returned to our sitting places. While we were like that, an old man came asking about the stoned man. We rose to him and seized him by his collar and brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: O Messenger of Allah, this one has come asking about the vile one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hush! He is more fragrant with Allah than the scent of musk! We left with the old man, and he turned out to be his father. We reached him and helped him with his washing, shrouding, and burial. He said: And I do not know whether he said prayer over him or not."
"17569","489 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shuaythi narrated, from Maslamah ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani, from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj, from his father, he said: We were boys working in the market. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding a man and he was stoned. A man came asking us about him, so we brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this one has come asking us about this vile one who was stoned today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say vile; by Allah, he is more fragrant with Allah than musk."
"17570","490 - Abu Zarah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, from Maslamah ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani, from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj, from his father, he said: We were boys hastening to the market. A man who had confessed to adultery was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was stoned. A man came asking us about the place of that man who was stoned. We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this one is asking us about that vile one. He said: Do not say vile; by Allah, he is more fragrant with Allah than musk."
"17571","491 - Abu Usamah Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, my father narrated. And Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated - they said: Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ala ibn al-Lajlaj narrated to me, from his father, he said: My father said to me: O my son, when I die, bury me in a side grave. When you place me in my grave, say: In the name of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah. Then sprinkle the soil upon me, then recite at my head the opening of al-Baqarah and its ending, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that."
"17572","Those named Labibah. Labibah al-Ansari. 492 - Al-Qasim ibn Abbad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited this verse: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness over these, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept and said: O Lord, this is what I witnessed over those among whom I live; so how about those whom I did not see?"
"17573","493 - Al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: A roasted sheep was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar. He and Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Marur ate from it, and they both fell severely ill. Then Bishr died. When he died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for the Jewess who had gifted it and said: What did you feed us, woe to you? She said: I fed you poison. He said: What drove you to that? She said: I heard you mention; if you were a prophet I knew it would not harm you, and if you were other than that I wanted to relieve people of you! Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding her and she was crucified."
"17574","The chapter of Mim. Those named Muhammad. Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari, a Badri; he resided in Madinah until he died there in the year forty-three at the age of seventy-seven. From his reports and mention of his age and death: 494 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Zaurah ibn Abd al-Ashhal: Muhammad ibn Maslamah ibn Khalid ibn Adi ibn Majdaah ibn Harithah ibn al-Harith."
"17575","495 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from al-Aws, from Banu Harithah: Muhammad ibn Maslamah."
"17576","496 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah: Muhammad ibn Maslamah ibn Khalid ibn Adi ibn Majdaah ibn Harithah ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj ibn Amr ibn Malik ibn al-Aws, and he was an ally of Banu Abd al-Ashhal."
"17577","497 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah died in Madinah in the year forty-three, at the age of seventy-seven years."
"17578","498 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah died in Safar in the year forty-three."
"17579","What Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated. Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 499 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Muhammad ibn Uthman, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: Some people of the Ansar passed by Muhammad ibn Maslamah while he was looking at a slave girl from Banu al-Najjar. They said: Glory be to Allah! If one of our youths did this we would consider it ugly! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts into a man's heart the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her - thus Yahya ibn al-Ala said, from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Uthman."
"17580","500 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, he said: I proposed to a woman and began to hide myself from her until I looked at her. It was said to him: Do you do this while you are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts into the heart of any of you the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her. Thus Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated it, and Yazid ibn Harun followed him."
"17581","501 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah pursuing the daughter of al-Dahhak with his gaze. I said: Glory be to Allah! You look at her while you are from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts into a man's heart the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her. Yahya ibn Said narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, as Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Yazid ibn Harun narrated it from al-Hajjaj."
"17582","502 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Musa ibn Shaybah al-Ansari narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sirmah narrated, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah al-Ansari, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah al-Ansari, he said: I was sitting with Muhammad ibn Maslamah when the daughter of al-Dahhak passed behind him, and he began to pursue her with his gaze. I said: Glory be to Allah! You do this while you are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts the proposal of a woman into a man's heart, there is no harm in looking at her."
"17583","503 - Yusuf ibn Yaqub the judge narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Jumahi narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his father, he said: I was sitting with Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari in his house when he saw an Ansari slave girl and followed her with his gaze. I said to him: May Allah have mercy on you! You look at her with this gaze! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts into a man's heart the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her. Thus Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated it from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his father."
"17584","504 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, al-Hajjaj narrated, from Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah pursuing Thubaytah bint al-Dahhak in one of the dwellings of Madinah with his gaze. I said: Do you do this? He said: Yes; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts into a man's heart the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her. Thus Abu Muawiyah narrated it from al-Hajjaj, from Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah."
"17585","505 - Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, he said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari see the daughter of al-Dahhak playing upon a wall, and he began to look at her. It was said to him: Do you look at her while you are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts into a man's heart the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her. Thus Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it, differing from the people in it. The narrators from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah differed in this hadith, and the correct view in my opinion - and Allah knows best - is what Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Yazid ibn Harun narrated from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah."
"17586","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 506 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from Urwah, that he narrated from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from Umar, a hadith concerning the miscarriage of a woman. Al-Mughirah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in it a slave as blood money. Umar said: If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that! So Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge in it a slave."
"17587","507 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Anas ibn Iyad narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that Umar consulted the people concerning the fetus a woman aborts. Al-Mughirah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in it a slave, male or female, as blood money. Umar said: If you are truthful, bring someone to testify with you! So Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge with it."
"17588","508 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafii al-Makki narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that Umar asked about the fetus. Al-Mughirah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in it a slave, male or female. Umar said: Who will testify with you if you are truthful? So Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge with that."
"17589","509 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki and Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab consulted the people concerning the miscarriage of a woman. Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge in it a slave, male or female. He said: Then bring me someone to testify with you! So he brought him Muhammad ibn Maslamah."
"17590","Qabisah ibn Dhuayb al-Khuzai from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 510 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb al-Khuzai, he said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr seeking her inheritance from her son or her daughter. Abu Bakr said: I find nothing for you in the Book of Allah, and I did not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree anything for you, and I shall ask the people in the evening. When he prayed Zuhr, he turned to the people and said: The grandmother came to me asking her inheritance from her son or her daughter, and I did not find anything for her in the Book, and I did not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree anything for her; so did any of you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning her? Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah stood and said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree for her a sixth. So Abu Bakr gave her a sixth. He said: Did anyone hear that with you? Muhammad ibn Maslamah stood and said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree for her a sixth. So Abu Bakr gave her a sixth. When the caliphate of Umar came, the grandmother who opposed her came to him. Umar said: The decree was only concerning other than you, but when you both are together, the sixth is between you both, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers."
"17591","511 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam informed us, Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman ibn Ishaq ibn Kharashah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, he said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq asking him her inheritance in the Book of Allah. Abu Bakr said to her: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I know nothing for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); return until I ask the people! He asked the people, and al-Mughirah ibn Shubah said: I was present when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her a sixth. Abu Bakr said: Is there anyone else with you? Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari stood and said the like of what al-Mughirah said. So Abu Bakr executed it for her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar ibn al-Khattab asking him her inheritance. He said: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and the decree that was decreed was only for other than you, and I shall not add anything in the obligatory shares; but it is that sixth: if you both are together in it, it is between you both, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers."
"17592","512 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated, Jarir narrated, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, he said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr and said: My son's son or my daughter's son has died, and it is mentioned that I have a right in what he left; so what is my right? Abu Bakr said: I know nothing for you in the Book of Allah, and I shall ask; return. When he prayed Zuhr, he said: Who heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning grandmothers? Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah said: I heard him. He said: How did you hear him? He said: He gave the grandmother a sixth. He said: Did anyone other than you know that? Muhammad ibn Maslamah stood and said: He spoke the truth; it is as he said. He said: So the woman came and he gave her a sixth. When Abu Bakr passed away, may Allah be pleased with him, and Umar was caliph, may Allah be pleased with him, a woman came to him in the like of that and said what the woman who spoke to Abu Bakr said. He answered her with the like of his saying, then he asked, and they said: Al-Mughirah said such and such, and Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified with him, so he gave her a sixth. And Umar said on his own part: When you both are together, it is for you both, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers."
"17593","Mahmud ibn Labid from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 513 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, from Salim ibn Salih ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I do when those who pray differ? He said: Go out with your sword to the Harrah and strike it with it, then enter your house until a decreed death comes to you or an erring hand."
"17594","Jafar ibn Mahmud ibn Maslamah from his uncle Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 514 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Dhuayb ibn Imamah narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning Banu Qurayzah, the Aws found that hard. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to every house of the houses of al-Aws two captives, and he sent to Banu Harithah two captives."
"17595","Abd al-Rahman al-Araj from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 515 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood to pray, would say: Allah is Greatest; I have turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, inclining, a Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed my prayer and my sacrifice and my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, with no partner for Him; with that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King; there is no god but You; glory be to You and with Your praise - then he would recite. When he bowed, he would say: O Allah, to You I bowed, in You I believed, to You I submitted, and upon You I relied; You are my Lord. All my hearing and my sight and my flesh and my blood and my brain have bowed to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Then he would raise his head and say: Allah hears whoever praises Him; our Lord, and to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter. When he prostrated, he would say: O Allah, to You I prostrated, in You I believed, to You I submitted; You are my Lord. My face prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it and split its hearing and its sight; blessed be Allah, the best of creators."
"17596","516 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated, Abu Haywah Shurayh ibn Yazid narrated, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from al-Araj, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his prostration: O Allah, to You I prostrated, in You I believed, to You I submitted, and You are my Lord. My face prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it and split its hearing and its sight; blessed be Allah, the best of creators. When he bowed, he would say: O Allah, to You I bowed, in You I believed, to You I submitted, upon You I relied; You are my Lord. My hearing and my sight and my blood and my brain and my bone and my sinew have humbled themselves to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Then he would raise his head from bowing and say: Allah hears whoever praises Him; our Lord, and to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter."
"17597","Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 517 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Ali ibn Zayd narrated, from Abu Burdah, he said: We passed by al-Rabadhah and there was a tent. I said: Whose is this? It was said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah's. I entered upon him and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muhammad ibn Maslamah, there will be tribulation and division and dissension. When that happens, break your sword, break your arrows, cut your bowstring, and sit in your house. The tribulation has occurred, and I did what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me. I turned and there was a sword hanging from the tent pole. I drew it and it was a sword of wood. He said: I did what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me, and I took this to frighten people with it."
"17598","Yusuf ibn Mihran from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 518 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Said ibn al-Musayyib ibn Sharik narrated, al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, that Muhammad ibn Maslamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: There will be division and tribulation and dissension. Strike with your sword the side of Uhud, and sit in your house until an erring hand comes to you or Allah grants you health."
"17599","Al-Muhajir from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 519 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated, al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated, a shaykh known as Abu Muhammad narrated, a shaykh called al-Muhajir narrated in the great mosque in the time of Khalid, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord has fragrant breezes in the days of your time, so expose yourselves to them; perhaps a breeze from them may strike you and you will never be wretched after it - and the wording is Ibrahim ibn Hashim's."
"17600","Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 520 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated, Harb ibn Maymun informed me, from al-Jald ibn Ayyub, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, he said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah said: I returned from a journey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand, and he did not release my hand until I released his hand."
"17601","Yunus ibn Abi Khaldah from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 521 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Quraysh ibn Hayyan narrated, from Yunus ibn Abi Khaldah, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat at the end of his affair, then prayed without performing ablution."
"17602","Al-Hasan al-Basri from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 522 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abbad ibn Musa al-Saadi narrated, Yunus narrated, from al-Hasan, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, he said: I passed by and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on al-Safa placing his cheek upon the cheek of a man. I went away, and it was not long before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: O Muhammad ibn Maslamah, what prevented you from greeting? Muhammad ibn Maslamah said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you doing with this man something you did with no one of the people, so I disliked interrupting your conversation. Who was he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It was Gabriel, peace be upon him, and he said: What is with Muhammad ibn Maslamah that he did not greet? Had he greeted, we would have returned the greeting upon him. He said: What did he say to you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He kept advising me concerning the neighbor until I expected he would command me to make him an heir."
"17603","523 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Sahl ibn Abi al-Salt narrated, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Ali sent to Muhammad ibn Maslamah and he was brought. He said: What kept you back from this affair? He said: Your cousin - meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - gave me a sword and said: Fight with it as long as the enemy is fought with it; when you see people killing one another, take it to a rock and strike it with it, then stay in your house until a decreed death comes to you or an erring hand. He said: Let him go."
"17604","An unnamed man from Muhammad ibn Maslamah. 524 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated, from Musa ibn Abdah, from al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from one of the children of Muhammad ibn Maslamah, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulations after me. If you encounter any of them, bring your sword to the side of the Harrah and strike it with it, join al-Rabadhah and be a master of camels until an erring hand kills you or a decreed death."
"17605","Muhammad ibn Safwan - and it is said Safwan ibn Muhammad, and the correct is Muhammad ibn Safwan. 525 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Safwan ibn Muhammad, that he came to his sheep and caught two hares and slaughtered them with a flint. He brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hanging them, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered them with a flint! He said: Eat them both."
"17606","526 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Safwan, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two hares, hanging them in his hand, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to sheep of mine and found these two hares, and I found no iron to slaughter them with, so I slaughtered them with a flint; may I eat them? He said: Yes."
"17607","527 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated, my father narrated. And al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Nasr al-Tusi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated - both said: Shubah narrated, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn Safwan, that he caught two hares and slaughtered them with a flint. He asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded him to eat them."
"17608","528 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn Safwan, he said: I slaughtered two hares with a flint. I brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded me to eat them."
"17609","529 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn Safwan, he said: I slaughtered two hares with a flint. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him and said: May I eat them? He said: Yes."
"17610","Muhammad ibn Sayfi al-Ansari. 530 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated. And Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated. And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Asad narrated - both said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim Abu Zayd narrated. And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated. And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Hulwani and Abu Kurayb narrated, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated - all of them from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn Sayfi al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us on the day of Ashura and said: Is there among you one who ate today? We said: Among us are those who ate and among us are those who did not eat. He said: Whoever did not eat, let him complete his fast; and whoever ate something, let him complete the rest of his day - then he sent to the people of al-Arud commanding them with that."
"17611","531 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Khalid narrated, Husayn narrated, from Amir, from Muhammad ibn Sayfi al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Ashura: Whoever of you ate, let him abstain for the rest of his day; and whoever did not eat, let him fast. And he sent to the people of al-Arud and commanded them to fast it."
"17612","532 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated, al-Hurr ibn Malik narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn Sayfi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his caller on the day of Ashura: Whoever is fasting, let him continue in his fast; and whoever ate and drank, let him complete his fast."
"17613","533 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated, al-Walid ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Harrani narrated, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn Sayfi, he said: I used to pasture sheep for my family in the ravine of Uhud, and I caught two young hares. I took a stone and slaughtered them with its edge - meaning its sharp side. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Eat it."
"17614","Muhammad ibn Hatib ibn al-Harith ibn Mamar ibn Habib ibn Wahb ibn Hudhafah ibn Jumah ibn Amr ibn Husays ibn Kab ibn Luayy al-Jumahi, and his mother is Fatimah bint al-Mujallil ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays ibn Abd Wudd ibn Nasr ibn Malik ibn Hisl; his mother emigrated with him to the land of Abyssinia. 534 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated, Waki narrated, from Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Hatib say: I was born in Abyssinia."
"17615","535 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib al-Jumahi narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: When my mother brought me from the land of Abyssinia after Hatib died, she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while one of my hands had been burned by fire. She said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Muhammad ibn Hatib, and this burn from the fire has afflicted him. Muhammad ibn Hatib said: I shall not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I do not know whether he blew upon my head or wiped it, and he supplicated for blessing in me and in my offspring."
"17616","536 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated - both from Shubah, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Hatib al-Jumahi say: Something from a pot spilled upon my hand, so my mother took me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said concerning it words: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind. And I think he said: Heal, and You are the Healer."
"17617","537 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: The pot fell upon my hand and it burned, so I was taken to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would spit lightly upon it and say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind. And I think he said: And heal, You are the Healer."
"17618","538 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: I drew near to a pot of ours while I was a small boy, and my hand burned. My mother caught up with me and brought me to a man at al-Batha. She said: O Muhammad, Muhammad's hand has burned! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to spit lightly upon it."
"17619","539 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated, Waki narrated, from Misar, from Simak ibn Harb, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: I drew near to a pot belonging to my mother and overturned it upon myself while I was a boy. My mother dragged me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he performed ruqyah upon me, saying: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer; there is no healer but You. He said: I did not retain the words, so I asked my mother about them, and she informed me in the time of Uthman."
"17620","540 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: I took hold of a pot of ours and my hand burned. My mother took me to a man in al-Jabbanah and said to him: O Messenger of Allah! He said: At your service and felicity. Then she brought me near him, and he began to blow and speak words I do not know what they were. I asked my mother after that what he used to say, and she said: He used to say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer; there is no healer but You."
"17621","541 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, he said: I was sitting with Muhammad ibn Hatib and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have seen a land with date palms, so go out. He said: So Hatib and Jafar set out by sea toward al-Najashi, and I was born in that ship."
"17622","542 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Balj, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The distinction between the lawful and the unlawful is the voice and the beating of the tambourine."
"17623","543 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib narrated, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is deprived of wife and child, he must engage in jihad."
"17624","Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah; he was born in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who named him Muhammad and gave him the kunyah Abu al-Qasim. 544 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Fahd ibn Awf Abu Rabiah narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Hilal al-Wazzan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Umar looked at Ibn Abd al-Hamid - and his name was Muhammad - while a man was saying to him: May Allah do with you, O Muhammad, and do! Reviling him. Umar called him and said: O Ibn Zayd, I do not see Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reviled on your account; by Allah, he shall never be called Muhammad as long as I live! So he named him Abd al-Rahman. He sent to Banu Talhah - and they were seven, their chief and eldest being Muhammad ibn Talhah - to change their names. Muhammad said: I remind you of Allah, O Commander of the Faithful; by Allah, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Muhammad! He said: Arise; there is no way to anything the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named."
"17625","Muhammad al-Saadi. 545 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, al-Awzai narrated, Muhammad ibn Khurashah narrated, Urwah ibn Muhammad al-Saadi narrated to me, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three things, when you see them, then beware, beware: the ruining of the inhabited, the inhabiting of the ruined, that raiding become a support, and that a man rub himself against his trust as a camel rubs against a tree."
"17626","Muhammad ibn Fadalah al-Ansari then al-Zafari. 546 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated. And Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Basri narrated, Yunus ibn Muhammad ibn Fadalah al-Zafari narrated, from his father - and he was of those who accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them in the mosque of Banu Zufar and sat upon the rock that is in the mosque of Banu Zufar today, accompanied by Abd Allah ibn Masud and Muadh ibn Jabal and some of his Companions. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a reciter, who recited until he reached this verse: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness over these. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept until his beard shook. He said: O Lord, I bore witness over those among whom I live; so how about those whom I did not see?"
"17627","547 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated. And Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzar al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated - both said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Idris ibn Muhammad ibn Anas ibn Muhammad ibn Fadalah narrated, my grandfather narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah when I was two weeks old. I was brought to him, and he wiped over my head and said: Name him by my name, but do not give him my kunyah. I was taken with him for the Farewell Pilgrimage when I was ten years old. He said: Muhammad lived long until his head turned white, but the spot of the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not turn white."
"17628","548 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Idris ibn Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Zafari narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that he attended with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Farewell Pilgrimage when he was ten years old and had a forelock."
"17629","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh ibn Riab al-Asadi. 549 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh ibn Riab ibn Yamar ibn Sabirah ibn Murrah ibn Kathir ibn Ghanm ibn Dudan ibn Asad ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar ibn Nizar, an ally of Banu Umayyah; his father's grandmother was Umaymah bint Abd al-Muttalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); his father was killed on the day of Uhud as a martyr; and his paternal aunt was Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17630","550 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, Abu Kathir the freedman of Muhammad ibn Jahsh informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by Mamar while he was sitting at his house by the market with his thighs uncovered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mamar, cover your thighs, for the two thighs are private."
"17631","551 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir - a freedman of Muhammad ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Jahsh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed - while I was with him - by Mamar with his thighs uncovered. He said: O Mamar, cover your thighs, for the thigh is private."
"17632","552 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated, from al-Ala, from Abu Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17633","553 - Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu al-Muafa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir the freedman of Muhammad ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Jahsh, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and passed by a man from Banu Adi uncovering his thigh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover your thigh, O Mamar, for it is of the private parts."
"17634","554 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir the freedman of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the market when he passed by Mamar at his door with his thigh uncovered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover your thigh, O Mamar, for it is of the private parts."
"17635","555 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir the freedman of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17636","556 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Rawh ibn Salah narrated, Yahya ibn Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Kathir the freedman of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled on his behalf; and there is no gold nor silver there - they are only good deeds and evil deeds."
"17637","557 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated, Abu Kathir the freedman of the Laythiyyin narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah? He said: Paradise. When he turned away, he said: Except debt; Gabriel, peace be upon him, just told me secretly."
"17638","558 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Duhaym narrated. And Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated. And Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated - both said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami narrated to me, from Abu Kathir the freedman of the Aslamiyyin, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh - and he had companionship - say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I fight in the path of Allah until I am killed? He said: Paradise. When the man turned away, he said: Bring him back to me. When he came, he said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, said: Unless he has debt upon him."
"17639","559 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from al-Ala, from Abu Kathir the freedman of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to me: If a servant were killed in the path of Allah while debt is upon him, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled on his behalf."
"17640","560 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Abu Kathir the freedman of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the courtyard of the mosque. He raised his head to the sky and said: Glory be to Allah! What severity has been sent down? We remained the rest of our day and our night. When morning came, I went early to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what severity has been sent down? He said: If a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, he would not enter Paradise while debt is upon him."
"17641","561 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Umari informed us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh narrated to me, from his father, that Zaynab bint Jahsh used to wash the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a brass basin. Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I saw that basin."
"17642","Muhammad ibn Abi Umayrah al-Muzani. 562 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Muhammad ibn Abi Umayrah - and he was from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: If a servant were dragged upon his face from the day he was born until the day he dies in old age in obedience to Allah, he would belittle that on the Day of Resurrection and would wish to increase as he increases in reward and recompense."
"17643","Those named Malik. Malik ibn al-Tayyihan, Abu al-Haytham al-Ansari, an Aqabi and Badri; he remained in Madinah until he died there in the year twenty. From his reports: 563 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from al-Aws, from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan, and he was a chief, and he witnessed Badr, and he was the first to pledge upon Islam at al-Aqabah."
"17644","564 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah from the Ansar: Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan, and he was a chief."
"17645","565 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan died in the year twenty, and his name is Malik."
"17646","566 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The first to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Aqabah was Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan. He said: O Messenger of Allah, between us and the people are ropes - and ropes mean alliances and covenants - so perhaps we shall cut them, then you will return to your people after we have cut the ropes and fought the people! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at his saying and said: Blood is blood; destruction is destruction. When Abu al-Haytham was pleased with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him, he turned to his people and said: O my people, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I bear witness that he is truthful. Today he is in the sanctuary of Allah and His security, amid his people and his clan. Know that if you bring him out, the Arabs will cast you off with a single bow. If your souls are content with fighting in the path of Allah and the loss of wealth and children, then invite him to your land, for he is truly the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). If you fear betrayal, then from now. Abd Allah said: We have accepted from Allah and from His Messenger what He gave us, and we have given you from ourselves what you asked us, O Messenger of Allah. Leave between us, O Abu al-Haytham, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we may pledge allegiance to him. Abu al-Haytham said: I am the first to pledge. Then they all pledged. Satan shouted from the top of the mountain and said: O assembly of Quraysh, these Khazraj and Aws are allying with Muhammad against fighting you. They were frightened at that and alarmed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let this voice not alarm you, for it is only the enemy of Allah, Iblis; none of those whom you fear hears it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and shouted at Satan, saying: O son of Azabb, this is your work, and I shall attend to you."
"17647","567 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated, from Yahya ibn Ubayd Allah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah narrated to me, he said: Isha once escaped me one night, and I tossed about, sleep not coming to me. I said: If only I went out to the mosque and prayed what was decreed for me! I did so, then leaned against a side of it. Umar entered, and when he saw me he did not recognize me and said: Who is this? I said: Abu Bakr. He said: What brought you out at this hour? I said: Hunger! He said: Nothing brought me out but what brought you out! It was not long before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered. When he saw our dark figures, he did not recognize them and said: Who are these two? Umar hastened before me and said: This is Abu Bakr, and this is Umar. He said: What brought you two out at this hour? We informed him of the news. He said: Nothing brought me out but what brought you two out. Come with us to the house of al-Waqimi. We came to the door and sought permission. The woman came out, and he said: Where is so-and-so? She said: He went to fetch sweet water for us from the garden of Banu Harithah. She opened the door and we entered. It was not long before he came carrying a waterskin upon his back until he hung it upon a stalk of the palm stalks. Then he came to us and said: Welcome and greetings; no visitors better than visitors who visited me tonight. Then he brought a cluster of unripe dates, and we began to select in the moonlight and eat. Then he took the knife and went among the sheep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Beware of the milch one - or he said: the one with milk. He slaughtered a sheep for us, skinned it, cut it into the pot, and ordered the woman, who kneaded and baked. Then he brought us tharid and meat, and we ate. Then he went to the waterskin, which the wind had shaken so it had cooled, and gave us to drink. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah! We went out, nothing bringing us out but hunger, then we did not return until we obtained this. This is of the bliss you will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection. Then he said to al-Waqimi: Do you have no servant to suffice you this? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah! He said: Look for the first captives that come to me, then come to me and I shall order a servant for you. It was not long before captives came to him, and he came to him. He said: What brought you? He said: Your appointment which you promised me! He said: Stand and choose from them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, be you the one to choose for me. He said: Take this boy and treat him well. He came to his wife and informed her of what he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what he said to him. She said: He has commanded you to treat him well! He said: And what is good treatment? She said: That you free him. He said: He is free for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"17648","568 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, they said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Riyashi narrated, Abd Allah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz narrated, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at noon and found Abu Bakr in the mosque. He said to him: What brought you out at this hour? He said: What brought you out brought me out, O Messenger of Allah. Umar ibn al-Khattab came, and he said: O son of al-Khattab, what brought you out? He said: What brought you two out brought me out! Umar sat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to speak to them both. Then he said: Is there strength in you both to go to these palms and obtain food and drink and fruit juice? We said: Yes. He said: Take us to the house of Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan al-Ansari. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked ahead of us, greeted and sought permission three times, while Umm al-Haytham behind the door heard his greeting, wanting the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to increase her in greeting. When he intended to turn away, Umm al-Haytham came out hurrying behind them and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I heard your greeting, but I wanted you to increase us in your greeting! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Good! Then he said: Where is Abu al-Haytham? She said: O Messenger of Allah, he is near; he went to fetch sweet water for us. Enter, for he will come shortly, if Allah wills. She spread for them a mat beneath the tree. Abu al-Haytham came, rejoicing in them, his eyes delighted with them. He climbed a palm and cut for them clusters. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Seek reward, O Abu al-Haytham. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you shall eat of its unripe dates and its ripe dates and its inferior dates. Then he brought them water and they drank. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is of the bliss you will be asked about. Abu al-Haytham rose to slaughter a sheep for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Beware of the milch one. Umm al-Haytham rose to knead and bake for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, laid their heads for the midday rest. They were awakened when their food had become ready. The food was placed before them, and they ate and were satisfied. Abu al-Haytham returned to them the remainder of the clusters, and they ate of its ripe dates and its inferior dates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted them and supplicated good for them."
"17649","569 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Muhammad al-Sirini narrated, Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at an hour in which he did not usually go out. Then Abu Bakr went out, and he said to him: What brought you out, O Abu Bakr? He said: Hunger brought me out! He said: What brought you out brought me out! He said: Then Umar went out, and he said to him: What brought you out, O Umar? He said: Hunger brought me out, by the One who sent you with the truth! Then some of his Companions walked to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to them: Come with us to the house of Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan. They set out, and when they reached the house of Abu al-Haytham, his wife said: Abu al-Haytham has gone to fetch sweet water for us; go around to the garden. She opened for them the garden door and they sat. Abu al-Haytham came, and his wife said to him: Do you know who is with you? He said: No. She said: With you are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions. He entered and tied his horse to a palm, then came to them, greeted them, welcomed them. Then he went to a picking basket of his and brought a cluster, picking ripe dates for them. He brought them to them and poured them before them. Then Abu al-Haytham reached for a small sheep of his in a corner of the garden to slaughter a ewe from it for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: As for one with milk, no. He took a sheep, slaughtered it, skinned it, cut it into pieces, cooked it with water and salt. Then he came to his wife and asked her: Do you have anything? She said: Yes; we have some barley we had set aside. They ground it between them, then she kneaded it and baked it. Abu al-Haytham broke it and poured over it that meat he had cooked. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, and they ate. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu al-Haytham, do you have no servant? He said: No; by the One who sent you with the truth, we have no servant. He said: When it reaches you that captives have come to us, come to us and we shall give you a servant. Captives came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu al-Haytham came to him while before him were two boys - or he said: two servants. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu al-Haytham, choose from them both - or he said: select from them both. Abu al-Haytham said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cautious until he bared his forearms, and said: The one consulted is trusted, O Abu al-Haytham; take this one. When Abu al-Haytham turned away with him, he said: O Abu al-Haytham, treat him well, for I have seen him pray. He said: Yes; we shall feed him from what we eat, clothe him from what we wear, and not burden him with work he cannot bear. Abu al-Haytham went to his family, and they rejoiced in him with great joy and said: Praise be to Allah who has provided us a servant to serve us and help us with our estate! Abu al-Haytham said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has enjoined me concerning him. His wife said: Yes; we shall feed him from what we eat, clothe him from what we wear, and not burden him with work he cannot bear! He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has enjoined me concerning him. His wife said: Glory be to Allah! A servant whom Allah and His Messenger have given us to serve us - do you wish to deprive us of him? Abu al-Haytham said to the boy: You are free for the sake of Allah; if you love to stay with us, we shall feed you from what we eat, clothe you from what we wear, and burden you with no work but what you can bear; and if you wish, go wherever you wish."
"17650","570 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Baghawi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, Shayban narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at an hour in which he did not go out and no one met him in it. Abu Bakr came to him, and he said: What brought you out, O Abu Bakr? He said: I went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to look upon his face and greet him. It was not long before Umar came, and he said: What brought you out, O Umar? He said: Hunger! He said: I have found some of what you find. Come with us to Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan al-Ansari - and he was a man with many horses and sheep, and he had no servant. They came to him but did not find him; they found his wife. He said: Where is your companion? She said: He went early to fetch sweet water from the channel of so-and-so. It was not long before he came with a waterskin, then put it down. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), clinging to him, ransoming him with his father and mother. He took them to the shade of his garden and spread for them a mat. Then he went to a palm and brought a cluster. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not select of its ripe dates? He said: I wanted you to partake of its ripe dates and its unripe dates. They ate and drank of that water. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: This, by the One in whose hand is my soul, is of the bliss you will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection: this cool shade, ripe dates with cool water upon them. Go and prepare food for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not slaughter one with milk. He slaughtered for them a young she-goat or a kid, then brought them and they ate. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have a servant? He said: No. He said: When captives come to us, come to us. Two heads with no third came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Choose them both. He said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He said: The one consulted is trusted; take this one, for I have seen him pray, and treat him with kindness. He came to his wife and narrated to her the account of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Nothing he intends by what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said is better than freeing him. He said: Then he is freed. Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman said: He is only asked about it who did not mention the name of Allah at its beginning and did not praise Allah at its end; as for whoever mentioned the name at its beginning and praised at its end, he has rendered its thanks."
"17651","571 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi narrated, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day, and there were Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. He said: What brought you two out of your houses? They said: Hunger! He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing brought me out but what brought you two out. Arise. They arose with him, and he came to a man of the Ansar; the Ansari was not there, and there was the woman. He said to her: Where is so-and-so? She said: He went to fetch sweet water for us. While he was like that, the Ansari came with a waterskin of water upon him. When he looked at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his two companions, he said: Allah is Greatest! No one of the people has guests more noble than our guests. He said: He hung the waterskin and cut for them a cluster containing unripe dates and ripe dates and dry dates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Had you selected? He said: Choose, O Messenger of Allah, before your eyes. He said: He took the knife, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Beware of the milch one! He slaughtered for them and they ate. When they finished, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: You shall be asked about this bliss on the Day of Resurrection: hunger brought you out of your houses, then you did not return until you obtained of this bliss."
"17652","572 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated. And Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated - both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar came to us. We fed them ripe dates and gave them water to drink. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is of the bliss you will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection."
"17653","What Malik ibn al-Tayyihan narrated. 573 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Shihab ibn Abbad al-Abdi narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah - the brother of Shaqiq ibn Abi Abd Allah, the freedman of al-Hasan ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Abi Talib - Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Judan narrated to me, from his grandmother, from Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted."
"17654","574 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Hannat narrated. And Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated - both said: Abu Usamah narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Malik ibn al-Tayyihan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Peace be upon you, ten good deeds are written for him; and whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, twenty good deeds are written for him; and whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, fifty good deeds are written for him."
"17655","Malik ibn Rabiah, Abu Usayd al-Ansari then al-Khazraji then al-Saidi, a Badri. 575 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Abu Usayd Malik ibn Rabiah ibn al-Budn ibn Amir ibn Awf ibn Harithah ibn Amr ibn al-Khazraj ibn Saidah ibn Kab ibn al-Khazraj ibn Harithah ibn Thalabah ibn Amr ibn Amir."
"17656","576 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Yazid ibn Hazim, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Abu Usayd al-Saidi lost his sight before the killing of Uthman. He said: Praise be to Allah who let me enjoy my sight during the life of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when Allah intended tribulation among His servants, He withheld my sight from it."
"17657","577 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Abu Usayd al-Saidi died - and his name is Malik ibn Rabiah - in the year thirty, at the age of ninety years."
"17658","What Abu Usayd narrated. Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi from Abu Usayd. 578 - Musa ibn Harun and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Hazim informed me, from Sahl ibn Sad, he said: Abu Usayd al-Saidi said to me after his sight had gone: O son of my brother, if you and I were now at Badr and Allah restored my sight, I would show you the mountain pass from which the angels came out upon us, without doubt or dispute."
"17659","Anas ibn Malik from Abu Usayd. 579 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Tanukhi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Abu Usayd al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best houses of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then Banu Saidah; and in all the houses of the Ansar there is good. Sad ibn Ubadah said: I see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has preferred others over us! He said: You have been preferred over many."
"17660","Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd from his father. 580 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abu al-Yaman al-Nabbal, from Shaddad ibn Abi Amr ibn Himas, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd al-Ansari, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was coming out of the mosque and men mingled with women in the road. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold back, for you are not to claim the middle of the road; keep to the edges of the road. A woman would cling to the wall, so that her garment would catch upon something of the wall from her clinging."
"17661","581 - Abu Zarah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr when we lined up for battle: If they come close to you, shoot them with arrows."
"17662","582 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated, al-Abbas ibn Sahl narrated to me, from his father and Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When they come close to you, shoot them with arrows."
"17663","583 - Abu Zarah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated - both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated, Abbas ibn Sahl and Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us with companions of his. We went out with him and proceeded until we reached a garden called al-Shawt, until we reached two gardens and sat between them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit here. The Jawaniyyah woman had been brought and secluded in the house of Umaymah bint al-Harith ibn Sharahil, with a midwife of hers. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, he said: Give yourself to me. She said: Would a queen give herself to a commoner? He extended his hand toward her to place it upon her. She said: I seek refuge in Allah from you! He said: You have sought refuge in a refuge! Then he came out to us and said: O Abu Usayd, clothe her with two linen garments and join her to her family."
"17664","584 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi narrated, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ishaq ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas narrated, my grandfather, my mother's father, Malik ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd al-Saidi, narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Usayd al-Saidi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: O Abu al-Fadl, do not leave your house, you and your sons, tomorrow until I come to you. They waited for him until he came after forenoon. He entered upon them and said: Peace be upon you. He said: And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. He said: How are you this morning? He said: Well; I praise Allah. He said: Draw near, draw near, draw near, each of you crawling to the other, until when they made room for him, he covered them with his cloak. Then he said: O Lord, this is my uncle and the twin of my father, and these are my household; shield them from the Fire as I shield them with this cloak of mine. He said: The threshold of the door and the walls of the house said amen: Amen, amen, amen."
"17665","585 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi narrated, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ishaq ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to me, he said: I heard from my mother's father Malik ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd narrating from his father, from his grandfather Abu Usayd al-Saidi al-Khazraji, he said - and he had a well in Madinah called the well of Budaah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had spat in it, and he rejoiced in it and sought blessing through it. He said: When Abu Usayd harvested the fruit of his garden, he placed it in a room of his. A ghoul would come to his storeroom in his absence, stealing his dates and spoiling them upon him. He complained of that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: That is the ghoul, O Abu Usayd; lie in wait for her. When you hear her rush - meaning her thud - say: In the name of Allah; the Messenger of Allah has detained me. The ghoul said: O Abu Usayd, excuse me from burdening me to go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I shall give you a covenant from Allah that I shall not come to your house in your absence nor steal your dates, and I shall guide you to a verse from the Book of Allah which you may recite over your house, and we shall not come to your family in your absence nor uncover its covering. She gave him the covenant he accepted from her. She said: The verse to which I guide you is Ayat al-Kursi. Then she scratched her buttocks, breaking wind. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and narrated to him the story when she turned away. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She spoke the truth, though she is a liar."
"17666","Al-Zubayr ibn Abi Usayd from his father. 586 - Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated. And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated - both said: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Hasan ibn Abi Hasan al-Barrad al-Madini narrated, my father Ali ibn Hasan narrated to me, al-Zubayr ibn Abi Usayd informed me, from his father, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, I have seen a place for a market; will you not look at it? He said: Yes. He rose with him until he came to the site of the market. When he saw it, it pleased him, and he struck it with his foot. Then he said: This market of yours is excellent; let it not be demolished, and let no tax be imposed upon it."
"17667","Yazid ibn Zayd from Abu Usayd. 587 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated, Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar narrated, from Yazid ibn Zayd, from Abu Usayd al-Saidi, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the grave of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. They began to draw the striped cloak over his face and his feet became exposed, and draw it over his feet and his face became exposed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Place it upon his face, and place upon his feet of this idhkhir. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head and his Companions were weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when they go out to the countryside, obtaining there food and clothing and mounts - or he said: mounts - and they will write to their families: Come to us, for you are in a barren land of little good, while Madinah is better for them, had they known. No one endures its hardship and its severity but I shall be for him an intercessor and a witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"17668","Ghaziyyah Abu Umarah from Abu Usayd. 588 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, from his father, that he narrated that some youths asked Abu Usayd about the preference the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the Ansar. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best tribes of the Ansar are the houses of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then Banu Saidah; and in all the Ansar there is good. Abu Usayd said: Had I said other than the truth, I would have begun with my grandfather; and Abu Usayd was Saidi."
"17669","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Usayd. 589 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that Abu Usayd, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best houses of the Ansar are the houses of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the house of al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then the house of Banu Saidah; and in all the houses of the Ansar there is good. Abu Usayd said: Had I lied, I would have begun with my people Banu Saidah. That reached Sad ibn Ubadah and he felt something in himself about that. He said: We were created and we were the least of the four? Saddle for me my donkey that I may come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! His nephew Sahl said to him: Would you go to refute the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Allah and His Messenger know best? He ordered his donkey unsaddled."
"17670","590 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Usayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu Saidah, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj."
"17671","Malik ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd from his grandfather. 591 - Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madini narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Abd al-Majid ibn Sahl, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil, from Malik ibn Hamzah, from Abu Usayd al-Saidi, that the people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the digging of the Trench pledging allegiance to him upon emigration. When he finished, he said: O assembly of Ansar, do not pledge upon emigration; people emigrate to you. Whoever meets Allah loving the Ansar shall meet Allah loving him, and whoever meets Allah hating the Ansar shall meet Allah hating him."
"17672","Ali ibn Ubayd from Abu Usayd. 592 - Abu Zarah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated - they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated, Usayd ibn Ali narrated to me, from his father Ali ibn Ubayd, the freedman of Abu Usayd, from Abu Usayd - and he was a Badri - he said: While I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of the Ansar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may I be dutiful to my parents after their death? He said: Yes; four traits: praying over them and seeking forgiveness for them, fulfilling their covenant after their death, honoring their friend, and maintaining the kinship through which you have kinship only from their side. He said: Then this is what remains upon me."
"17673","Qurrah ibn Abi Qurrah from Abu Usayd. 593 - Musa ibn Harun and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, they said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Aban ibn Yazid narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated, that Qurrah ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us that Abu Usayd narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no prayer after the Asr prayer."
"17674","Irak ibn Malik from Abu Usayd. 594 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Muaddib narrated, Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Habib al-Misri narrated to me, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Usayd al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining dates and raisins."
"17675","Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki Muhammad ibn Muslim from Abu Usayd. 595 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, he said: I heard Abu Usayd al-Saidi while Ibn Abbas gave a fatwa permitting a dinar for two dinars. Abu Usayd spoke and harshened speech to him. Ibn Abbas said: I did not think that anyone who knows my kinship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to me such as this, O Abu Usayd. Abu Usayd said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Dinar for dinar, dirham for dirham, a sa of wheat for a sa of wheat, a sa of barley for a sa of barley, a sa of salt for a sa of salt; no excess between anything of that. Ibn Abbas said: This is something I used to say by my opinion, and I heard nothing in it."
"17676","596 - Ata al-Shami from Abu Usayd - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Ata - not Ibn Abi Rabah - from Abu Usayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat olive oil and anoint with olive oil, for it is a blessed tree."
"17677","597 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki narrated, from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Ata al-Shami, from Abu Usayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat olive oil and anoint with it, for it is from a blessed tree."
"17678","Malik ibn Sasah al-Ansari. 598 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Malik ibn Sasah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me about the night he was taken by night."
"17679","599 - Ali ibn Ahmad al-Abbar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Malik ibn Sasah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Malik ibn Sasah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abd al-Aziz al-Harmali narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Kab informed us, my father narrated, from al-Khalil ibn Murrah, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Malik ibn Sasah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Dawud narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Malik ibn Sasah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was in al-Hatim - and perhaps he said: in al-Hijr - between sleep and wakefulness, a comer came to me and I was split from the throat to the lower belly, and my heart was taken out. Then I was brought a basin of gold, and it was washed with Zamzam water and filled with wisdom and faith. I was brought a mount smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey, white, called al-Buraq, whose stride reaches its farthest glance. I was carried upon it. I set out, I and Gabriel, peace be upon him, until we came to the lowest heaven. Gabriel, peace be upon him, sought opening. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Welcome; what an excellent coming has come. It was opened for us and we entered. I came upon Adam and greeted him. He said: Welcome to you, of a son and a prophet. Then we came to the second heaven. Gabriel, peace be upon him, sought opening. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Welcome to him; what an excellent coming has come. It was opened for us, and I came upon Isa and Yahya and greeted them both. They said: Welcome to you, of a brother and a prophet. Then we came to the third heaven. Gabriel, peace be upon him, sought opening. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. They said: Has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Welcome to him; what an excellent coming has come. I came upon Yusuf and greeted him. He said: Welcome to you, of a brother and a prophet. Then we came to the fourth heaven. Gabriel, peace be upon him, sought opening. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. They said: Has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Welcome to him; what an excellent coming has come. He said: I came upon Idris and greeted him. He said: Welcome to you, of a brother and a prophet. Then we came to the fifth heaven. Gabriel, peace be upon him, sought opening. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. They said: Has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Welcome to him; what an excellent coming has come. I came upon Harun and greeted him. He said: Welcome to you, of a brother and a prophet. Then we came to the sixth heaven. Gabriel, peace be upon him, sought opening. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. They said: Has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Welcome to him; what an excellent coming has come. I came upon Musa and greeted him. He said: Welcome to you, of a brother and a prophet. When I passed him, he wept. It was said: What makes you weep? He said: O Lord, this one was sent after me; more of his nation will enter Paradise than will enter of my nation! Then we came to the seventh heaven. Gabriel, peace be upon him, sought opening. They said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. They said: Has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Welcome to him; what an excellent coming has come. I came upon Ibrahim and greeted him. He said: Welcome to you, of a son and a prophet. Then Sidrat al-Muntaha was raised for us. I asked Gabriel, peace be upon him, and he said: This is Sidrat al-Muntaha; its fruits are like jars, its leaves like elephant ears. I saw at its base four rivers: two outward rivers and two inward rivers. I asked Gabriel, peace be upon him, and he said: As for the two inward, they are two rivers in Paradise; as for the two outward, they are the Nile and the Euphrates. Then al-Bayt al-Mamur was raised for us. I asked Gabriel, peace be upon him, and he said: This is al-Bayt al-Mamur; seventy thousand angels enter it every day, then never return to it, the last of them. Fifty prayers were prescribed upon me. I set out until I came upon Musa, peace be upon him. He said: What did you do? I said: Fifty prayers were prescribed upon me. He said: I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the hardest treatment, and your nation will not bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. I returned and asked Him to lighten for me, and He made them forty prayers. I came upon Musa, peace be upon him, and he said: What did you do? I said: He made them forty. He said: I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the hardest treatment, and your nation will not bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. I returned and asked my Lord, and He lightened ten from me. I came upon Musa and he said: What did you do? I said: He made them thirty. He said: I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the hardest treatment, and your nation will not bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. I returned and asked Him to lighten them from me, and He made them twenty. I came upon Musa and he said: What did you do? I said: He made them twenty. He said: I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the hardest treatment, and your nation will not bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. I returned to my Lord and asked Him to lighten for me, and He made them fifteen. I came upon Musa and he said: What did you do? I said: He made them fifteen. He said: I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the hardest treatment, and your nation will not bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. I returned to my Lord and asked Him to lighten for me, and He made them ten. I came upon Musa and he said: What did you do? I said: He made them ten. He said: I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the hardest treatment, and your nation will not bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. I returned to my Lord and asked Him to lighten for me, and He removed five from me. I came upon Musa and he said: What did you do? I said: He removed five from me. He said: I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the hardest treatment, and your nation will not bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. I said: I have grown shy; how often shall I return to my Lord? I am content and I submit! It was called out: I have carried out My prescription and lightened for My servants, and I reward a good deed ten times its like."
"17680","600 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar narrated, Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated, Hammam narrated, Qatadah narrated, from Anas, from Malik ibn Sasah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night, I did not pass any angel among the angels but they commanded me with cupping."
"17681","Malik ibn Rabiah, Abu Maryam al-Saluli. 601 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from his father, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey. We alighted at a stop and slept past the prayer until the sun rose. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, ordered Bilal, who called the adhan. They performed ablution and prayed two rakahs, then Bilal gave the iqamah and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer. Then he narrated to us what will be until the Day of Resurrection; whoever retained it retained it, and whoever forgot it forgot it."
"17682","602 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated - both said: Jarir narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept at the face of dawn and did not wake until the sun rose. He awoke, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who called the adhan, then he prayed two rakahs, then he ordered and prayed Fajr."
"17683","603 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated - both said: Jarir narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in a standing, then narrated to us what will be until the Hour comes."
"17684","604 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, Hibban ibn Yasar al-Kilabi narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Maryam narrated, that he heard his father Abu Maryam mention from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that in a sermon of his: O Allah, forgive those who shave. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten! Three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And those who shorten."
"17685","605 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Raja ibn Muhammad al-Udhri narrated. And Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated - both said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated, Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Malik ibn Rabiah al-Saluli narrated to me, Yazid ibn Malik narrated, from his father, that he witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Day of the Tree and the Day of the Sacrifice held back before reaching its place, and that a man of the polytheists said: O Muhammad, what drives you to bring these against us while we dislike it? He said: These are better than you and than your forefathers; they believe in Allah and the Last Day. By the One in whose hand is my soul, Allah has been pleased with them."
"17686","Malik ibn Nadlah al-Jushami. 606 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a man and he did not host me nor entertain me; then he passed by me - shall I entertain him? He said: Rather entertain him."
"17687","607 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw upon me tattered clothes. He said: Do you have wealth? I said: Yes. He said: Of what wealth? I said: Of every kind Allah has given me. He said: Then let the blessing of Allah and His generosity be seen upon you."
"17688","608 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was unkempt in appearance. He said: Do you have wealth? I said: Yes. He said: Of what wealth? I said: Of every kind Allah has given me: of camels and horses and slaves and sheep. He said: When Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are the camels of your people born with sound ears, then you take to the razor and cut their ears and say: These are Buhur, and slit their skins and say: These are Surum, forbidding them for yourself and your family? I said: Yes. He said: All that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, gave you is lawful for you; the forearm of Allah is stronger than your forearm, and the razor of Allah is sharper than your razor. I said: O Messenger of Allah, consider a man I stayed with who did not honor me nor entertain me, then he stayed with me - shall I repay him for what he did? He said: No; rather entertain him."
"17689","609 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Israil narrated. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw me in poor appearance. He said to me: Do you have wealth? I said: Yes; of every wealth Allah has given me: of camels and cattle and horses and slaves. He said: When Allah gives you good, let the blessing of Allah and His generosity be seen upon you. I said: O Muhammad - and I had not yet accepted Islam that day - consider: if I stayed with a man and he did not entertain me nor recognize my right, then time befell him and he stayed with me - shall I repay him for what he did or entertain him? He said: No; rather entertain him. Then he said to me: Are your camels born with full ears? I said: Are camels born but so? He said: Then you take the razor and cut their ears and say: These are Buhur? You take your razor and slit their ears and say: These are Surum? I said: We do that! He said: Do not do it; all that Allah gave you is lawful. The razor of Allah is sharper than your razor, and the forearm of Allah is stronger than your forearm. He said: The best of the Arabs for that were Qays. And the wording is the hadith of Ibn Raja."
"17690","610 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an inferior garment. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes; Allah has given me of every wealth. He said: Of what wealth? He said: Allah has given me of horses and slaves. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When Allah gives you wealth, let the trace of His blessing and His generosity be seen upon you. Then he said: Are your camels born with full ears? He said: Are they born but so? He said: Then you take to your razor and cut the tips of the ears and say: These are Buhur? And slit a portion and say: These are Surum? He said: I do that! He said: Do not do it, for all that Allah gave you is lawful for you. Then he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he had not accepted Islam: O Muhammad, consider: if I stayed with a man and he did not host me nor recognize my right, then time brought him to me - shall I entertain him or repay him? He said: Rather entertain him."
"17691","611 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two shabby cloaks, and he said: Do you have any wealth? I said: Yes, every kind of wealth. He said: Then let the blessing of Allah be seen upon you! So I came to him in the morning wearing a red suit."
"17692","612 - Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi narrated, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated, from al-Ajlah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing poor clothes and in a bad state, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have any wealth? He said: Yes, every kind of wealth. He said: Then let what Allah has granted you be seen upon you."
"17693","613 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas who said: My father entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing worn-out clothes, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have any wealth? He said: Allah has given me every kind of wealth, camels, cattle and sheep. He said: Then let what Allah has given you be seen upon you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if I pass by a man and he refuses to host me, then time brings him in need to me, should I host him or withhold? He said: Rather, host him."
"17694","614 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, that Awf ibn Malik - meaning his father - came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing rags, and he said: O Awf ibn Malik, are not your camels born with sound ears, then you deliberately cut some of them and say: This is a Bahirah, and you deliberately slit some of them and say: These are Surum? Do not do so; the arm of Allah is stronger than your arm, and the knife of Allah is sharper. All that Allah has given you is lawful, and do not forbid anything of your wealth. Then he said to him: O Awf ibn Malik, is the servant who obeys you and follows your command more beloved to you, or your servant who does not obey you nor follow your command? He said: Rather, my servant who obeys me and follows my command. He said: Likewise you are with your Lord, the Exalted."
"17695","615 - al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated, Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat narrated, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began asking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his bad state he said: Do you have any wealth? He said: Yes, Allah has given me all wealth, camels, sheep and horses. He said: When Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you."
"17696","616 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Muhammad ibn Yazid informed us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was in a bad state, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have any wealth? I said: Yes, Allah has given me every kind of wealth. He said: If you have wealth, let it be seen upon you."
"17697","617 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a Bedouin manner upon me and wearing Bedouin clothes, and he said to me: Do you have wealth? He said: I said: Allah has given me every kind of wealth. He said: When Allah gives you wealth, let the trace of Allah's blessing be seen. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man harms me, should I do to him as he does to me? He said: No, for the upper hand is better than the lower hand. Then he said: What do you do with your camels, do you cut their ears and say Bahirah and Saibah and Wasilah? I said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The knife of Allah is sharper than your knife, and the arm of Allah is stronger than your arm."
"17698","618 - al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us, Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Zubaydi narrated, Abu Qurrah narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw him in a bad state, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you not have wealth? He said: He said: Yes indeed. He said: Then let the blessing of Allah be seen upon you."
"17699","619 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Humayd ibn Masadah narrated, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated, Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing worn-out clothes, and he said: Do you have wealth? I said: Yes, Allah has given me every kind of wealth, and he mentioned horses, camels, slaves and sheep. He said: When Allah gives you good, let it be seen upon you. He said: Are your camels born with complete ears? He said: So you take your knife and say, these are Buhur and these are Surum? He said: Yes. He said: All that Allah has given you is lawful, and the arm of Allah is stronger, and the knife of Allah is sharper."
"17700","620 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Janadi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was unkempt in appearance, and he said to me: Do you have any wealth? I said: Yes, camels, sheep and slaves. He said: Why is it not seen upon you?"
"17701","621 - al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mansur al-Qadi narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unkempt and in a bad state, and he said: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes. He said: What is your wealth? He said: Camels, horses and slaves. He said: When Allah gives you wealth - or he said: good - let it be seen upon you, for when Allah honors a servant He loves that His honoring him be seen. He said: Are your camels born with sound ears? He said: Are camels ever born without ears? He said: So you deliberately take a knife and cut their ears and say: These are Buhur, and slit their ears and say: These are Surum, and forbid them to yourself? I said: Yes. He said: All that Allah has given you is lawful, and the arm of Allah is stronger than your arm, and the knife of Allah is sharper than your knife! I said: O Prophet of Allah, I come to a man who does not host me nor honor me, should I repay him or host him? He said: Rather, host him."
"17702","622 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, Abu al-Zara Amr ibn Amr narrated, from his uncle Abu al-Ahwas, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he looked me up and down and said: An owner of camels or an owner of sheep? He said: Allah has given me of each, much and good. He said: You breed them with complete eyes and ears, then you cut this one and say: Sarma - then Sufyan said a word I did not understand - and you say: Bahirat Allah; and the arm of Allah is stronger, and the knife of Allah is sharper, and if He willed to bring it to you as Sarma He would bring it. I said: To what do you call? He said: To Allah and kinship. I said: A man from my cousins comes to me and I swear not to give him, then I do! He said: Expiate your oath and do what is better. Have you seen, if you had two slaves, one of them obeys you and neither betrays you nor lies to you, and the other betrays you and lies to you, is the one who obeys you and does not lie to you more beloved to you, or the one who betrays you and lies to you? I said: No, rather the one who does not betray me nor lie to me and tells me the truth is more beloved to me. He said: Likewise you are with your Lord."
"17703","623 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him disheveled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin, and said to him: What wealth do you have? He said: Allah has given me every kind of wealth. He said: When Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves that it be seen upon him."
"17704","624 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muammar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated, Amir ibn Mudrik narrated, Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, from his father and Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned similar to it."
"17705","Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, Abu Sulayman al-Laythi. 625 - Abu Man Thabit ibn Nuaym al-Hawji narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated (h). And Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn Hubab narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated (h). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated (h). And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated (h). And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated - they said: Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, Nasr ibn Asim narrated, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said takbir would raise his hands when entering the prayer until he brought them level with his ears, and when he bowed and when he raised his head from bowing. And the wording is one."
"17706","626 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he entered the prayer would raise his hands to the lobes of his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."
"17707","627 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said takbir would raise his hands until he brought them level with his ears, and when he raised his head from bowing he did likewise."
"17708","628 - Ahmad ibn Bishr ibn Habib al-Bayruti narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bakkar narrated, Said ibn Bashir narrated, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he said takbir until he brought them level with his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."
"17709","629 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated, my father narrated to me (h). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated, Qatadah narrated, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said takbir would raise his hands until he made them close to his ears, and when he bowed he did likewise, and when he raised his head from bowing he did likewise."
"17710","630 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated (h). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated - both said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands until he brought them level with the lobes of his ears. Yazid ibn Zuray added: And when he bowed likewise, and when he raised his head from bowing likewise."
"17711","631 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhallab ibn al-Ala narrated, Shuayb ibn Bayan narrated, Imran al-Qattan narrated, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he said takbir, and when he intended to bow, and when he raised his head from bowing, toward his ears."
"17712","632 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated (h). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated (h). And Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sawwar al-Anbari narrated (h). And al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated - they said: Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated, Yazid ibn Maysarah narrated, Abu Atiyyah - a freedman of ours - narrated, he said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith used to come to our prayer place, and the prayer was established, so we said to him: Step forward and lead! So he said to us: Put forward a man from among you to lead you, and I will tell you why I do not lead you; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever visits a people should not lead them, but let a man from among them lead them."
"17713","633 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated (h). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated - both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Abu Qilabah, that Malik ibn al-Huwayrith said to his companions: Shall I not show you how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was? And that was outside the time of prayer, so he stood, then bowed and said takbir, then raised his head and stood a little while, then prostrated, then raised his head, then waited, then prostrated, then raised his head, then waited a little while, then prostrated. And the wording is that of Arim."
"17714","634 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah who said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith came to us in our mosque and led us in prayer, and said: I pray with you though I do not intend the prayer, but I intend to show you how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray. Ayyub said: So I said to Abu Qilabah: How was his prayer? He said: Like the prayer of our shaykh Amr ibn Salamah, and the shaykh would complete the takbir, and when he raised his head from the first rakah he would lean upon the ground then stand."
"17715","635 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated (h). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated - they said: Hammad narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were young men, and we stayed with him about twenty nights or days, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: If you return to your families - or he said: your lands - teach them. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was merciful; order them to pray such-and-such prayer at such-and-such time and such-and-such prayer at such-and-such time, and when the prayer comes let one of you call the adhan then let the eldest of you lead you. And the wording is that of the hadith of Arim."
"17716","636 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eldest in age leads the people. And Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, when he raised his head from the second prostration, would sit then rise."
"17717","637 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among people while we were young men close in age, and we stayed with him twenty nights, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was merciful, gentle and forbearing, and he thought that we missed our families and longed for them, so he asked us about those we left behind and we informed him, so he said: Return to your families and stay with them and teach them and command them, and he said: When the prayer comes let one of you call the adhan and let the eldest of you lead you."
"17718","638 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated (h). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated - both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are with your companion, call the adhan and the iqamah, and let the elder of you two lead you."
"17719","639 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith who said: Two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending travel, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you two go out, call the adhan then the iqamah, and let the elder of you two lead you."
"17720","640 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him and to a companion of his: When the prayer comes, call the adhan then the iqamah, and let the elder of you two lead you."
"17721","641 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him and to a companion of his: When the prayer comes, call the adhan then the iqamah, and let the elder of you two lead you. So I said to Abu Qilabah: Where is the recitation? So he said: They were close in age."
"17722","642 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Abd al-Wahhab narrated (h). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah who said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith used to come to us and say: Shall I not tell you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then he would pray outside the time of prayer, and when he raised his head from the second prostration in the first rakah he sat upright then stood, leaning upon the ground."
"17723","643 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated, Sulayman ibn Muhammad al-Qafillai narrated, from Asim al-Jahdari, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us to recite: Then on that Day none will punish as He punishes, and none will bind as He binds."
"17724","644 - Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated (h). And Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani and Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr al-Hadhdha narrated to us, both said: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated - both said: Unays ibn Sawwar al-Jarmi narrated, my father narrated, Malik ibn al-Huwayrith narrated, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends to create a person, when the man has intercourse with the woman his fluid flies into every vein and nerve of hers, then on the seventh day Allah - Mighty and Majestic - brings for him every vein between him and Adam, then he recited: In whatever form He willed, He put you together."
"17725","645 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd ibn Masadah narrated, Unays ibn Sawwar Abu Ziyad al-Jarmi narrated, he said: My father said: I and Abu Qilabah were sitting at the back of the mosque, then Malik ibn al-Huwayrith entered upon us and said: Shall I not tell you how your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray? We said: Yes - so he stepped forward and bowed two short rakahs, then I and Abu Qilabah differed about his knees; I said: He stuck them to the ground, and Abu Qilabah said: He kept them apart."
"17726","646 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Umar ibn Aban narrated, Malik ibn al-Husayn ibn Malik ibn al-Huwayrith narrated, my father informed me, from my grandfather Malik ibn al-Huwayrith who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master."
"17727","647 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Imran ibn Aban narrated, Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Malik ibn al-Huwayrith narrated, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa."
"17728","648 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Imran ibn Aban narrated, Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Malik ibn al-Huwayrith narrated, from his father who said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith said: The first to accept Islam among men was Ali, and among women Khadijah."
"17729","649 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Imran ibn Aban narrated, Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Malik ibn al-Huwayrith narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended a step of the pulpit and said: Amen, then ascended another step and said: Amen, then ascended another step and said: Amen, then said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: O Muhammad, whoever reaches his parents or one of them then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him; say: Amen, so I said: Amen; and whoever reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance him; say: Amen, so I said: Amen; and whoever is mentioned before him and does not invoke blessings upon you, may Allah distance him; say: Amen, so I said: Amen."
"17730","650 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzar al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Ayli narrated, Imran ibn Aban narrated, Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Malik ibn al-Huwayrith al-Laythi narrated, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise, and their father is better than them."
"17731","Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Khuzai. 651 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated (h). And Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan narrated (h). And Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated - they said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from Mansur ibn Hayyan, from Sulayman al-Khuzai, from his maternal uncle Malik ibn Abd Allah who said: I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I never prayed behind an imam of a people whose prayer was lighter than that of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17732","652 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated, from Mansur ibn Hayyan, Sulayman ibn Bishr al-Khuzai narrated, from his maternal uncle Malik ibn Abd Allah who said: I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we never prayed behind an imam whose obligatory prayer was lighter than his."
"17733","Malik, Ubayd and Qays, sons of al-Khashkhash al-Anbari. 653 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Hurr ibn Husayn narrated, Nasr ibn Hassan narrated to me, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, that his father Malik and his two uncles Qays and Ubayd, sons of al-Khashkhash, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him about a man from their cousins raiding the people, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for them: This is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to Malik, Ubayd and Qays, sons of al-Khashkhash; you are safe Muslims regarding your blood and your wealth, you shall not be taken for the offense of another, and none shall wrong you except your own hands."
"17734","Malik ibn Ukhaymir. 654 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me (h). And Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misraf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated - both said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai narrated, from Abu Razin al-Bahili, from Malik ibn Ukhaymir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not accept from al-Saqqur any obligatory or voluntary act. It was said: What is al-Saqqur, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one who brings a man in upon his family."
"17735","Malik ibn Umayr al-Sulami. 655 - Ali ibn Ishaq al-Wazir al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz al-Makki narrated, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Abu Sakhr Wasil ibn Yazid al-Sulami then al-Nasiri narrated, my father and my uncles narrated to me, from my grandfather Malik ibn Umayr, that he was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest, Khaybar and Taif, and he was a poet, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, give me a ruling about poetry! So he said: That what is between your throat and your shoulder be filled with pus is better than that it be filled with poetry. I said: O Messenger of Allah, wipe over my head! So he placed his hand upon my head, and I did not say a verse of poetry after that. And Malik lived long until his head and beard turned white, but the place of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not turn white."
"17736","Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Ghafiqi, Abu Musa. 656 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Luhayah narrated, from Thalabah ibn Abi al-Kanud, from Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Ghafiqi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate food one day then said: Conceal me until I bathe. So I said: Were you in a state of major impurity, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, so I told that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: This one claims that you ate while you were in a state of major impurity? So he said: Yes, when I perform ablution I eat and drink, but I do not pray nor recite until I bathe."
"17737","657 - Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Yahya ibn Maymun al-Ghafiqi - a man from Ghafiq - from Abu Musa al-Ghafiqi, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: This companion of yours is preserving yet perishing; the last of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to us when he said: Whoever preserves something from me, let him narrate it; and whoever deliberately lies upon me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"17738","658 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Luhayah narrated, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Yahya ibn Maymun, that Wadaah al-Hamdi narrated to him that he was beside Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Ghafiqi while Uqbah ibn Amir was narrating, so Malik said: This companion of yours is heedless and perishing; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to us in the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: Hold to the Quran, for you will return to a people who desire narration from me; so whoever understands something, let him narrate it, and whoever fabricates upon me, let him take a seat - or something - in Hell - I do not know which of the two he said."
"17739","Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Khathami. 659 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated, Damrah narrated, from Raja ibn Abi Salamah, from Hassan, freedman of Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Khathami - and Malik was among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: I saw Malik ibn Abd Allah performing ablution, and there was a vein in his leg written for Allah, so I kept looking at it, and he said: What are you looking at? It was not written by a writer."
"17740","660 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqbah al-Maafiri informed me, from his father, that he heard Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Khathami narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like the hadith of Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream will see me in wakefulness, and Satan does not take my form."
"17741","661 - Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhlham al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr and Ibn Jabir, from Abu al-Musabbih, from Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Khathami, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whose feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"17742","Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani. 662 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, both said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Zaynab narrated to me, that Malik ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani passed by Habib ibn Maslamah - or Habib ibn Maslamah passed by Malik - while he was leading his horse and walking, so he said to him: Why do you not ride, since Allah has given you a mount? So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whose feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"17743","Malik ibn Buhaynah al-Azdi, Abu Abd Allah; Buhaynah is his mother, Buhaynah bint al-Harith ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf, sister of Ubaydah ibn al-Harith; he is Malik ibn Said ibn al-Qishb of Azd Shanuah. 663 - Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Muqri al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, from his father, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Malik ibn Buhaynah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man praying while the prayer had been established, so he spoke to him something I do not know what it was; then when we finished we gathered around him saying: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to you? He said: He said: It is likely that the dawn prayer will be prayed as four."
"17744","Malik ibn Haydah al-Qushayri. 664 - Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Qazah, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father, that he said to his brother Malik ibn Haydah: Take us to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he knows you and does not know me, and he has detained some people of Banu Bahdam, my neighbors; so they came to him and Malik ibn Haydah said: O Messenger of Allah, I have accepted Islam and my neighbors have accepted Islam, so release them! But he did not answer him, then he repeated to him but he did not answer him, then he repeated to him but he did not answer him, so he stood up angrily and said: If you do that, they claim that you call to a matter yet turn to other than it; so I kept rebuking him and forbidding him, and he said: What is he saying? They said: He says such-and-such, so he said: If you do that, that is upon me what is upon them of it; leave his neighbors for him."
"17745","Malik ibn Hubayrah al-Sakuni. 665 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abd Allah al-Yazani, from Malik ibn Hubayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim over whom three rows pray but it becomes incumbent. He said: And Malik, when he faced the people of a funeral, would divide them into three rows."
"17746","Malik ibn Amr al-Qushayri. 666 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Malik al-Qushayri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a Muslim slave, it is his ransom from the Fire; a bone of his freed one for a bone of his bones."
"17747","667 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Malik ibn Amr al-Qushayri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever reaches one of his parents then is not forgiven, may Allah distance him; and whoever takes an orphan between parents to his food and drink until Allah enriches him, Paradise becomes incumbent for him."
"17748","668 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Shubah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from a man of his people called Malik or Abu Malik who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes an orphan among Muslims to his food and drink until he becomes independent of him, Paradise becomes incumbent for him necessarily; and any man who reaches his parents or one of them then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him; and any Muslim man who frees a Muslim slave, it is his ransom from the Fire."
"17749","669 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Malik ibn Amr ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes an orphan between two Muslim parents until he becomes independent, Allah has made Paradise incumbent for him necessarily."
"17750","670 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Hushaym narrated, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Malik ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes an orphan among Muslims to his food and drink until he becomes independent of him, Paradise becomes incumbent for him necessarily; and whoever frees a Muslim person, it is his ransom from the Fire, each limb of his ransoming a limb of him."
"17751","Malik ibn Atahiyah. 671 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Luhayah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muhsin ibn Dhibyan, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan; a man of Judham informed me that he heard Malik ibn Atahiyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If you meet a tithe-collector, kill him - meaning thereby charity taken without right."
"17752","Malik ibn Awf al-Nasri, kunya Abu Ali. 672 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated: Malik ibn Awf ibn Sad ibn Rabiah ibn Yarbu ibn Wathilah ibn Dahman ibn Nasr ibn Muawiyah ibn Bakr ibn Hawazin. Ibn Sallam said: Malik ibn Awf al-Nadri was a leading chief; his first mention and famed valor was on the day of al-Fijar with his people, great was his deed that day; and he was over Hawazin when he met them with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he drove with the people their wealth and offspring; Durayd ibn al-Simmah opposed him, persisted and refused, so they went with his view and did not praise his opinion; he was their chief that day; then when he saw the defeat of his companions he aimed at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he was fiercely daring - to strike him, as claimed! Then Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi met him and killed him, and he spurred his horse to charge but it did not advance, then he wanted him and shouted at him but it did not advance. Then he was present after accepting Islam at al-Qadisiyyah. Then he fled from Hunayn and went to Taif; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he comes to me I will grant him safety and give him a hundred; so he came and he did that for him and directed him to fight the people of Taif. And Sad ibn Abi Waqqas wrote to Umar - may Allah be pleased with him - seeking reinforcements, so he wrote to him: Do you seek my reinforcement while you are among ten thousand and with you are Malik ibn Awf and Hanzalah ibn Rabiah, he who was called Hanzalah the Scribe. Ibn Sallam said: One of his people narrated to me that he said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me seeking to reconcile me to Islam, but I did not wish to take a wage for Islam, so I return it. He said: He only gave it while deeming it rightfully yours."
"17753","673 - Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the delegation of Hawazin at Hunayn, and he asked them about Malik ibn Awf al-Nadri: What did Malik do? They said: He is at Taif. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Inform Malik that if he comes to me as a Muslim I will return to him his family and wealth and give him a hundred camels. So Malik was brought that news and he came out to him from Taif; and Malik feared Thaqif for himself lest they know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said to him what he said and detain him; so he ordered a mount of his to be prepared, and ordered a horse of his to be brought to him from Taif, and he went out at night, mounted his horse and caught up with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reaching him at al-Jiranah or Makkah; so he returned to him his family and wealth and gave him a hundred camels."
"17754","Malik, Abu al-Saib, grandfather of Ata ibn al-Saib. 674 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Rashid ibn Sallam al-Ahwazi narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam al-Sulami narrated, from Muhammad ibn Tammam, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a well in which there was a dead black man; he said: So he looked into the well, and he was cast in the well; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Why is he cast in the well? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he was harsh in religion, praying sometimes and sometimes not praying! He said: Woe to you, take him out! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him washed and shrouded, and said: Carry him. And he said: The angels nearly preceded us! He said: And he prayed over him."
"17755","675 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Rashid ibn Sallam narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam al-Sulami narrated, from Muhammad ibn Tammam, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is prompted at death with the testimony that there is no god but Allah enters Paradise."
"17756","676 - And with its chain, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave people to benefit from one another; and when your brother seeks your advice, advise him."
"17757","Those named Mahmud. Mahmud ibn Maslamah al-Ansari, brother of Muhammad ibn Maslamah, martyred on the day of Khaybar. 677 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Luhayah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: Among the naming of those martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Muslims, then from the Ansar, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Mahmud ibn Maslamah."
"17758","678 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: Among the naming of those martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah: Mahmud ibn Maslamah. And they mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muhammad ibn Maslamah: Your brother has the reward of two martyrs. And Allah knows best."
"17759","The age of Muawiyah and his death, and some of his reports: 679 - Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan died with four nights remaining of Rajab in the year sixty; Ibn Kathir said: And his age was between seventy and eighty."
"17760","680 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, Abu Zayd Umar ibn Shabbah narrated, from Abu Nuaym who said: Muawiyah died in the year sixty, and his age was between seventy and eighty."
"17761","681 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali, from Jarir, that he heard Muawiyah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-three years old; and Abu Bakr and Umar; and I am sixty-three years old."
"17762","682 - Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan who said: Muawiyah was tall, fair and bald."
"17763","683 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated, Muslim ibn Jundub narrated, from Aslam, freedman of Umar, who said: Muawiyah came to us while he was the fairest and most handsome of people."
"17764","684 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from his father who said: I saw Muawiyah at al-Abtah with white head and beard like snow."
"17765","685 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Minhab ibn Abbad al-Abdi narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid al-Hamdani narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi who said: Muawiyah went out from Sham intending Makkah, and stopped at a place between Makkah and Madinah called al-Abwa, and looked into an ancient well and was struck by facial paralysis; so he hastened until he reached Makkah, and the chamberlain came to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, the people are at the door, I miss no face! He said: Then spread for me. He said: Then he called for a turban and wrapped his head with it and split his face, then went out and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, if I recover, the righteous before me have recovered, and I would not be pleased that I hope to be among them; and if a limb of mine has sickened, I cannot count my sound ones; and if some of your elite hold against me, I was at war against your commoners; and I have no right to wish from Allah more than what He has given me; so may Allah have mercy on a man who supplicates for my well-being; so voices rose with supplication and he wept; so Marwan said to him: What makes you weep, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I reconsidered what I had turned away from; my age has grown, my bone has thinned, tears have increased in my eye, and I have been struck in my best and what appears of me; and were it not for a desire of mine regarding Yazid, I would have seen my right course."
"17766","686 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, al-Mualla al-Qaqa'i narrated, Muhammad ibn Habib al-Khawlani narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai who said: I was napping in a church at Ariha, and it was then a mosque prayed in; he said: So Awf ibn Malik woke from his sleep, and with him in the house was a lion walking toward him; so he stood frightened to his weapon, so the lion said to him: Wait, I was only sent to you with a message to convey! I said: Who sent you? He said: Allah sent me to you to inform Muawiyah the traveler that he is among the people of Paradise! I said: Which Muawiyah? He said: Ibn Abi Sufyan."
"17767","687 - Qays ibn Muslim al-Bukhari narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Thabit, freedman of Abu Sufyan, narrated, he said: I fought alongside Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan in the land of Rome, and a crack occurred in his saddle, so he called: O servants of Allah, the Muslims! So the first to answer was Muawiyah; so he dismounted and the people dismounted, and they said: We suffice the commander; so he said: Indeed it has reached me that the first to aid is Jibril, so I wished to be the second."
"17768","688 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm who said: Ali said: My slain and the slain of Muawiyah are in Paradise."
"17769","689 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated, he said: I heard Abu Usamah say: I heard Mujalid ibn Said say: May Allah have mercy on Muawiyah, how intense was his love for the Arabs."
"17770","690 - al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays who said: Muawiyah said to his brother: Ride behind, but he refused; so he said: Evil is how you were disciplined; so Abu Sufyan said: Leave your brother."
"17771","691 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated, I heard Abu Yahya al-Himmani say: I heard al-Amash say: If you saw Muawiyah you would say: This is the Mahdi."
"17772","What Muawiyah, may Allah have mercy on him, transmitted; the Companions from him; what Ibn Abbas narrated from Muawiyah, may Allah have mercy on them. 692 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Hisham ibn Hujayr narrated, from Tawus who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: This is a proof against Muawiyah, his statement: I trimmed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a Bedouin arrow-head at al-Marwah, when he says: When he forbids mutah."
"17773","693 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, al-Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I trimmed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during his umrah at al-Marwah with an arrow-head."
"17774","694 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Muawiyah who said: I trimmed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Marwah with an arrow-head during his hajj."
"17775","695 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from Muawiyah who said: I trimmed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Marwah with an arrow-head."
"17776","696 - Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Shiyami narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from Muawiyah who said: I trimmed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Marwah with a Bedouin arrow-head."
"17777","697 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated (h). And Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated - both said: Marwan ibn Shuja narrated, Khusayf narrated, from Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that Muawiyah informed him that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shorten his hair with an arrow-head; we said to Ibn Abbas: We have not heard this except from Muawiyah; so Ibn Abbas said: Muawiyah was not suspect regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17778","698 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Yaish narrated, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: Muawiyah said to me: Have you seen one who performed tamattu and drove the sacrificial animal, does he touch anything of his hair? So I said: No. He said: I bear witness that I took from the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Marwah when he finished his tawaf, with an arrow-head from his quiver."
"17779","699 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn narrated, from Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade wearing gold."
"17780","700 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn narrated, from Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade wearing jewelry and gold."
"17781","Abu Said al-Khudri from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with them both. 701 - Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated (h). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated - both said: Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Attar narrated, Abu Naamah narrated, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: Muawiyah went out to a circle in the mosque and said: What has seated you? They said: We sat remembering Allah. He said: By Allah, nothing seated you but that? They said: By Allah, nothing seated us but that. He said: I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you, and there was none in my position relative to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who narrated less from him than I; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to a circle of his companions and said: What has seated you? They said: We sat remembering Allah and praising Him for guiding us to Islam and bestowing you upon us. He said: By Allah, nothing seated you but that? They said: By Allah, nothing seated us but that. He said: I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you; Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and informed me that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, boasts of you to the angels."
"17782","Abu al-Darda from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with them both. 702 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, Bishr ibn Jabalah narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, that Abu al-Darda said a word by which Allah benefited Muawiyah; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not pry into people, lest you corrupt them."
"17783","Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali from Muawiyah. 703 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from Abu al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Jarir, from Muawiyah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty-three; and Abu Bakr passed away when he was sixty-three; and Umar passed away when he was sixty-three."
"17784","704 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad, from Jarir, from Muawiyah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty-three."
"17785","705 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah who said: I heard Muawiyah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-three; and Abu Bakr died when he was sixty-three; and Umar died when he was sixty-three."
"17786","706 - Ahmad ibn Masud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated (h). And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Sadan ibn Yazid narrated, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated, Sharik ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Shabi, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, from Muawiyah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty-three; and Abu Bakr passed away when he was sixty-three; and Umar passed away when he was sixty-three."
"17787","al-Numan ibn Bashir al-Ansari from Muawiyah. 707 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated, Musa ibn Umar al-Hazimi narrated, from Musa ibn Sahl, from Yazid ibn al-Numan ibn Bashir, from his father, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has placed the truth upon the tongue and heart of Umar."
"17788","Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As from Muawiyah. 708 - al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated, Abu al-Mutarrif al-Mughirah ibn Mutarrif al-Wasiti narrated, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Muawiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of Ashura and said: This is a day whose fasting was not prescribed upon you; and I am fasting; so whoever wishes to fast, let him fast; and whoever wishes to break, let him break."
"17789","Wail ibn Hujr al-Hadrami from Muawiyah. Abu Amir al-Ashari from Muawiyah. 709 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated (h). And Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr al-Ataki narrated - both said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Maladh, from Numayr ibn Aws, from Malik ibn Masruh, from Amir ibn Abi Amir al-Ashari, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What a good tribe are al-Azd and the Asharis! So Muawiyah said: Not so! He said: He only said: They are from me and to me."
"17790","Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with them both. 710 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated, Said ibn Bishr narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr said to Muawiyah in the exchange that occurred between them regarding the pledge to Yazid: And you, O Muawiyah, informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there are two caliphs on earth, kill one of them."
"17791","Usayd ibn Zuhayr from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with them both. Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with them both. 711 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, Aban ibn Yazid narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, that Muawiyah said: When you come to my pavilion, stand among the people and inform them what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The merchants are the wicked. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, did not Allah permit trade? So he said: They speak and lie, and swear and sin."
"17792","al-Saib ibn Yazid from Muawiyah. 712 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us (h). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, Umar ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me, that Nafi ibn Jubayr sent him to al-Saib ibn Yazid asking him about something Muawiyah saw of him in prayer; so he said: I prayed with him Friday in the enclosure; then when he gave salam I stood in my place and prayed; then when he entered he sent to me and said: Do not repeat what you did; when you pray Friday do not join it to a prayer until you speak or go out, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that. Hawdhah added in his hadith: That it not be joined to a prayer until you speak or go out."
"17793","713 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, my brother narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, from his father who said: Muawiyah sent to me after Asr and said: Where were you? I said: I was praying; so he said: Do you pray after Asr? So I said: Yes; so Muawiyah said: Do not do so, for I know better about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17794","714 - Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Dawud ibn Ata narrated, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, from his father, that he informed him that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan forbade the two rakahs prayed after Friday in the mosque and the two rakahs after Asr; Muawiyah says: And I know best about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17795","715 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated (h). And Abu Ghassan Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Sukkari al-Ahwazi narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated - both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, my father narrated to me, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that he heard Muawiyah delivering a sermon at Madinah upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a lock of hair in his hand; so he said: Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid this, and he said: Those before you were only destroyed when their women adopted it."
"17796","716 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated (h). And Abu Ghassan Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated - both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, my father narrated to me, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that he heard Muawiyah delivering a sermon saying: O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This is the day of Ashura, and Allah did not prescribe its fasting; and I am fasting; so whoever loves to fast, let him fast; and whoever loves to break, let him break."
"17797","Sabrah ibn Mabad al-Juhani from Muawiyah. 717 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr Abu Jafar al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Mabad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah al-Juhani narrated, my uncle Harmalah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Sabrah ibn Mabad who said: Imran ibn Husayn said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Juhaynah is from me and I am from them; they anger at my anger and are pleased at my pleasure; I anger at their anger and am pleased at their pleasure; so whoever angers them has angered me, and whoever angers me has angered Allah. So Muawiyah said to him: He only said this hadith regarding Quraysh. So Imran said: I heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while you that day were dead."
"17798","Yazid ibn Jariyah al-Ansari from Muawiyah. 718 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari narrated (h). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, from Yahya ibn Said, Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Yazid ibn Jariyah al-Ansari who said: We were sitting around the couch of Muawiyah, then he came out to us and said: What were you discussing? They said: We were in a narration from the narrations of the Ansar. So Muawiyah said: Shall I not add for you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."
"17799","Muawiyah ibn Hudayj from Muawiyah. Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him. 719 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Mujammi ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated, Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated to me, he said: I heard Muawiyah, when the muadhdhin said takbir twice he said takbir twice, and when he testified twice he testified twice. Then he turned to me and said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say at the adhan."
"17800","720 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Mujammi al-Ansari, that he heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, when he heard the muadhdhin say takbir he said takbir and testified with what he testified, then said: Thus Muawiyah narrated to us that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say as the muadhdhin said; then when he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah - he said: And I bear witness. Then he fell silent."
"17801","721 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Uthman ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf who said: I heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf say: I heard Muawiyah while he was seated upon the pulpit, then the muadhdhin called: Allah is Greatest; so Muawiyah said: Allah is Greatest; then he mentioned like it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17802","722 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated, Jarir narrated, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Mujammi ibn Yahya, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf who said: I heard Muawiyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he heard the muadhdhin and said like what he said."
"17803","Those who narrated from Muawiyah among the Followers of Madinah. Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Muawiyah. 723 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan narrated (h). And al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated - both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam who said: I entered with Muawiyah upon Aishah, Mother of the Believers, and she said: O Muawiyah, you killed Hujr and his companions, and did what you did; did you not fear that I would hide for you a man to kill you for Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr? He said: No, I am in a house of safety; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith restrains treacherous killing; a believer does not kill treacherously. O Mother of the Believers, how am I regarding your needs, your messengers and your affair? She said: Good; he said: Then leave me and Hujr until we meet before Allah."
"17804","724 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khali al-Himsi narrated, my father narrated, from Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, from Mubashshir ibn Ubayd, from Bishr ibn Ubayd, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from his father, from his grandfather, from Muawiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that men stand up for him when they see him approaching, let him take a house in the Fire."
"17805","Said ibn al-Musayyib from Muawiyah. 725 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-zur, and al-zur is that a woman joins her hair."
"17806","726 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Muawiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-zur."
"17807","727 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yaqub ibn al-Qaqa, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that Muawiyah said: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade you al-zur; then he came with a black rag and cast it before them, then said: This is it, which a woman places in her head then covers over it."
"17808","728 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib who said: Muawiyah came to Madinah and stood upon the pulpit with a lock of hair in his hand, and said: I did not think anyone did this, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called it al-zur."
"17809","729 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated, from Said ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion."
"17810","Alqamah ibn Waqqas al-Laythi from Muawiyah. 730 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Alqamah ibn Waqqas, from his father who said: I was sitting with Muawiyah; then when the muadhdhin called and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, Muawiyah said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; then the muadhdhin said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, so Muawiyah said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; then the muadhdhin said: Come to prayer, so Muawiyah said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah; then he said: Come to success, so Muawiyah said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah; then he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, so Muawiyah said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; then he said: There is no god but Allah, so Muawiyah said: There is no god but Allah; then Muawiyah said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17811","731 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The muadhdhin called the adhan in the presence of Muawiyah, so he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; so Muawiyah said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; then he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; then he said: Come to prayer; he said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah; he said: Come to success; he said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah; he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; Muawiyah said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; then he said: There is no god but Allah; so he said: There is no god but Allah; then he said: Thus I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"17812","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Muawiyah. 732 - Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Luhayah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that he heard Muawiyah upon the pulpit of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a lock of hair, and he said: I found this among my family, and they claim that women add it to their hair; and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah curses the woman who joins hair and the one joined."
"17813","Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah from Muawiyah. 733 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated (h). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Umra is permissible for its people."
"17814","734 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ibn Mubarak narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Muawiyah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Umra is permissible."
"17815","735 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Rawh ibn Salah narrated, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from his uncle, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Umra is like inheritance."
"17816","Isa ibn Talhah from Muawiyah. 736 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Muawiyah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The longest-necked of people are the muadhdhins."
"17817","737 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Isa ibn Talhah who said: We entered upon Muawiyah, then the caller called for prayer and said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; so Muawiyah said as he said; then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, so he said likewise also; then he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, so he said likewise; then he said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"17818","Musa ibn Talhah from Muawiyah. 738 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Maysarah ibn Habib, from Musa ibn Talhah who said: I witnessed Uthman delivering a sermon upon the pulpit standing, and witnessed Muawiyah delivering a sermon seated; so he said: I did not ignore the Sunnah, but my age has grown, my bone has thinned and your needs have increased; so I wished to fulfill some of your needs while seated, then stand and take my share of the Sunnah."
"17819","739 - Qays ibn Muslim al-Bukhari narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Muawiyah ibn Isa narrated, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated, from Musa ibn Talhah who said: I entered upon Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan; then when I went out he called me and said: Listen, I have a hadith, O son of my brother, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow."
"17820","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Muawiyah. 740 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he saw Muawiyah delivering a sermon upon the pulpit with a lock of hair in his hand; he said: So I heard him say: Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the like of this, and he said: The Children of Israel were only punished when their women adopted this."
"17821","741 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan with a lock of hair in his hand saying: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the like of this, and say: The Children of Israel were only punished when their women adopted this."
"17822","742 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated, from Malik (h). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Malik informed us (h). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Malik narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan in the year he performed hajj, while upon the pulpit, taking a lock of hair that was in the hand of a guard, saying: O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the like of this and say: The Children of Israel were only destroyed when their women adopted this. And the wording is that of the hadith of al-Qanabi."
"17823","743 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Tinnisi narrated, al-Awzai narrated, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan with a lock of hair in his hand saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the like of this and say: The Children of Israel were only destroyed when their women adopted it."
"17824","744 - Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan delivering a sermon upon the pulpit at Madinah saying: Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the like of this lock, saying: The Children of Israel were only destroyed when their women adopted it."
"17825","745 - Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj and Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, both said: Said ibn Ufayr narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan with a lock of hair in his hand saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the like of this and say: The Children of Israel were only punished when their women adopted the like of this."
"17826","746 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan with a man, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the like of this and say: The Children of Israel were only destroyed when their women adopted this."
"17827","747 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: Muawiyah came to Madinah and said: Where are your scholars? And he brought out a tuft of hair from his sleeve and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid this, and he said: The Children of Israel were only destroyed when their women adopted the like of this."
"17828","Chapter. 748 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that he heard Muawiyah delivering a sermon saying: O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This is the day of Ashura and its fasting was not prescribed upon us; so whoever among you wishes to fast, let him fast, for I am fasting; so the people fasted."
"17829","749 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Qanabi narrated, from Malik (h). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Malik informed us (h). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muawiyah on the day of Ashura in the year he performed hajj, while upon the pulpit, saying: O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This day is the day of Ashura, and its fasting was not prescribed upon you; and I am fasting; so whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break."
"17830","750 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated (h). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated - both said: Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: Muawiyah came to Madinah and said: Where are your scholars? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on this day and said: I am fasting; so whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break."
"17831","751 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muawiyah while upon the pulpit saying in his sermon: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This day is the day of Ashura, and its fasting was not prescribed upon you; and I am fasting; so whoever loves, let him fast it - meaning the day of Ashura."
"17832","752 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan delivering a sermon on the day of Ashura and saying: O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This is the day of Ashura, and its fasting was not prescribed upon you; and I am fasting; so whoever loves to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever loves to break, let him break."
"17833","753 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sad narrated, my uncle narrated, my father narrated, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him that he heard Muawiyah addressing the people on the day of Ashura saying: O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This is the day of Ashura, and its fasting was not prescribed upon you; and I am fasting - and he was saying that - so whoever among you loves to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever loves to break, let him break."
"17834","754 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Malik ibn Sad al-Qaysi narrated, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muawiyah upon the pulpit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This is the day of Ashura, and its fasting was not prescribed upon you; and I am fasting; so whoever wishes, let him fast; and whoever wishes, let him break."
"17835","Chapter. 755 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Bakr, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am only a distributor, and Allah gives."
"17836","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17837","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain from this ummah a community standing firm upon the command of Allah; those who oppose them will not harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are dominant upon the truth."
"17838","756 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17839","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him. 757 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Muawiyah performed Hajj and prayed two rakahs, then when he came in to him it was said to him: No one has criticized your cousin as you have been criticized. He said: What is that? They said: You prayed two rakahs while Uthman prayed four. He said: I prayed two rakahs with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they kept pressing him until he went out and prayed four."
"17840","Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Muawiyah. 758 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, that Amr ibn al-As said to Muawiyah: O Commander of the Believers, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, when he was building the mosque, to Ammar: You are indeed keen upon jihad, and you are indeed among the people of Paradise, and the rebellious party will kill you? He said: Yes. He said: Then why did you kill him? He said: By Allah, you keep slipping in your urine; did we kill him? The one who brought him is the one who killed him."
"17841","759 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, that he heard Amr ibn al-As, Abdullah ibn Amr, and Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar: The rebellious party will kill you."
"17842","760 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Hanzalah al-Sadusi, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, and Muawiyah was his maternal uncle, who said: I was with Muawiyah after the Asr prayer, and he saw people praying two rakahs after it, so he said: What is this prayer? We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we never saw anyone pray it."
"17843","Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Muawiyah. 761 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in a single garment."
"17844","Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As from Muawiyah. 762 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abu Hassan al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Muhammad ibn al-Saib al-Kalbi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As narrated to us, from his father, who said: Muawiyah used to say: By Allah, I never feared speaking before anyone as I feared it before Aishah, and I never heard her speech except that it reminded me of the speech of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17845","Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar from Muawiyah. 763 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hadrami, from Salim ibn Abdullah, that Muawiyah kept saying to some of those present: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said such-and-such? They said: Yes. He said: Did he not say concerning tamattu and Umrah, forbidding it? Those who affirmed the first hadith said: No, by Allah, he did not say this, nor do we know that he said it."
"17846","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Muawiyah. 764 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, both saying: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people: If the imam prays sitting, then pray sitting. Al-Qasim said: So the people marvelled at the truthfulness of Muawiyah."
"17847","Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from Muawiyah. 765 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father Abbad ibn Abdullah, who said: We performed Hajj with Muawiyah in the year he performed Hajj, and he prayed Zuhr as two rakahs, then Marwan ibn al-Hakam and Amr ibn Uthman entered upon him and said: What is this prayer? He said: This is a sunnah which I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. They said: Your cousin used to complete it as four. He said: I remember nothing but this."
"17848","Humran ibn Aban from Muawiyah. 766 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Humran saying: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan addressed us and said: You indeed pray a prayer which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never used to pray, and he used to forbid it, meaning the two rakahs after Asr."
"17849","Dhakwan Abu Salih al-Samman from Muawiyah. 767 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Dhakwan, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him, he said it three times; then if they drink a fourth time, kill them."
"17850","768 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf al-Jubari narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he drinks wine, flog him; he said at the fourth time: kill him."
"17851","769 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Muawiyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies without a pledge of allegiance upon his neck dies a death of ignorance."
"17852","770 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Dhakwan, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the muadhdhin saying Allahu Akbar, he would say the like of his saying; then when he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, he would say the like of his saying; then when he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice, he would say the like of his saying."
"17853","771 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Muawiyah, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speaking while Bilal was giving the adhan; when he said: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, the Prophet of Allah said: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, the Prophet of Allah said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; then he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it, then fell silent."
"17854","Yusuf Abu Muhammad, freedman of Uthman, from Muawiyah. 772 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from his father, from Muawiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets anything in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"17855","773 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, narrated to him, from his father, that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan led them in prayer and forgot, so he stood while he owed a sitting and did not sit; then at the end of his prayer he prostrated two prostrations before the taslim, then said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"17856","774 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to me, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, that Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to him that Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to him, from his father, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he led them in prayer and forgot, so he stood while he owed a sitting and did not sit; then at the end of the prayer he prostrated two prostrations before giving salam, then said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"17857","775 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of Uthman, saying: When the muadhdhin gave the adhan, Muawiyah would say the like of what he said until he reached his saying: Come to prayer, come to success, whereupon he would say: There is no power nor strength except through Allah, then he would say the like of what he said, then he said: This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"17858","776 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, that Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to him that Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to him, from his father, that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan led them in prayer and forgot, so he stood while he owed a sitting and did not sit; then at the end of his prayer he prostrated two prostrations before giving salam, then said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"17859","777 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qawwas narrated to us, Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu Bakr narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of Amr ibn Uthman, from his father Yusuf, that he saw Muawiyah lead the people in prayer and stand up in the two rakahs, so the people said Subhan Allah, and he gestured to them to stand; then when he finished his prayer he prostrated two prostrations before the salam, and the people prostrated them with him, then he said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is overcome by doubt in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"17860","778 - Al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from his father, from Muawiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets anything in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations."
"17861","Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Muawiyah. 779 - Abu Usamah Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim used to narrate, saying: It reached Muawiyah that Abdullah ibn Amr was narrating that there would be a king from Qahtan, so Muawiyah became angry, stood, praised Allah as He deserves, then said: To proceed, it has reached me that men among you relate narrations that are neither in the Book of Allah nor transmitted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and those are your ignorant ones; beware of fancies that mislead their people, for I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This authority is in Quraysh; none opposes them except that Allah throws him down upon his face, as long as they uphold the religion."
"17862","780 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir al-Bakhtari al-Himsi narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Muawiyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This authority is in Quraysh; none opposes them except that Allah throws him down upon his face, as long as they uphold the religion."
"17863","781 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, who said: It reached Muawiyah that Abdullah ibn Amr was narrating, mentioning that there would be a king from Qahtan, so he became angry and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This authority will remain in Quraysh; none opposes them except that he is thrown down upon his face, as long as they uphold the religion."
"17864","Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi from Muawiyah. 782 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik. And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Yazid ibn Ziyad, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, who said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said, while upon the minbar: O people, there is none to withhold what Allah gives, nor any giver of what He withholds, nor does the fortune of the fortunate avail him against Him; and whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion. Then he said: I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon these sticks."
"17865","783 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Yala narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad, freedman of Ali ibn Abi Talib, narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi narrated to me, who said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan came to us, ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, there is none to withhold what Allah gives, nor any giver of what He withholds, nor does the fortune of the fortunate avail him against Him; and whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17866","784 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi narrated to me, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan addressing in Medina, saying: You shall surely know, O people, that there is none to withhold what Allah gives, nor any giver of what Allah withholds, nor does the fortune of the fortunate avail him against Him; whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion. I heard these letters from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon these sticks."
"17867","785 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj al-Riyashi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Amr narrated to us. And Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, both saying: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, who said: I heard Muawiyah addressing, saying: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion; and this wealth is green and sweet, so whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it. Then he says: I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the minbar; and the hearing obedient one has no argument against him, while the hearing disobedient one has no excuse."
"17868","786 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Rashid, from Muhammad ibn Kab, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion, and inspires him with his right guidance."
"17869","787 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Kab saying: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, there is none to withhold what You give, nor any giver of what You withhold; whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17870","788 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Kufi narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Kab, that a group in the time of Muawiyah would attend Fajr and sit with the storyteller of the congregation, then when he finished they would move to a corner of the mosque and remember Allah and recite the Book of Allah until the day grew high; so Muawiyah was informed of them, and he came hurrying, or hastening in his walk, until he stood over them and said: I have come to give you glad tidings of the glad tidings of Allah in what He has granted you: that a group in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - I think he said - used to do similar to what you do, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came forward, as if I am depicting him in his walk, until he stood over them and said: Rejoice, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah Almighty boasts of you to the angels."
"17871","Al-Numan ibn Murrah al-Zuraqi from Muawiyah. 789 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Numan ibn Murrah al-Zuraqi, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the Ansar, it is through my love that he loves them; and whoever hates the Ansar, it is through my hatred that he hates them."
"17872","Muhammad ibn Uqbah, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, from Muawiyah. 790 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Uqbah, who said: Muawiyah addressed and spoke something the people disapproved of, and they answered him back, and that pleased him; and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be rulers who speak and are not answered back, plunging into the Fire, one following another."
"17873","Ayyub ibn Bashir al-Ansari from Muawiyah. 791 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ayyub ibn Bashir ibn al-Numan al-Ansari, Muawiyah narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until he ascended the minbar, mentioned the martyrs of Uhud, prayed over them at length, then said: A servant among the servants of Allah was given a choice by Allah between this world and what is with Him, and he chose what is with Allah; none grasped it except Abu Bakr, who said: We would ransom you with our fathers and mothers. He said: Gently, O Abu Bakr; the best of people to me in companionship and in wealth is the son of Abu Quhafah."
"17874","Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab from Muawiyah. 792 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubashshir al-Madini, the companion of Ibn Abi Dhib, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab, who said: Muawiyah stood upon the minbar and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17875","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who inserts into her head hair that is not her own hair only inserts falsehood."
"17876","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh, the most caring toward a husband in his means, and the most tender toward a child in his childhood."
"17877","Mahmud ibn Ali al-Qurazi from Muawiyah. 793 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, from Mahmud ibn Ali al-Qurazi, that when the muadhdhin gave the adhan, Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan would say Allahu Akbar like his takbir, and testify like his testimony; then when he said: Come to prayer, come to success, he said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah. This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"17878","Al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab from Muawiyah. 794 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr Abu Jafar al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Azhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Jafari narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I am not of idle amusement, nor is idle amusement of me."
"17879","Fadl al-Madani from Muawiyah. 795 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Fadl, who said: I heard Muawiyah, and with him was a lock of womens hair, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever adds to his hair anything that is not of it only adds falsehood to it."
"17880","Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Muawiyah. 796 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani narrated to us, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan in Medina, with a lock of womens hair in his hand, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the like of this, and said: The women of the Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted this."
"17881","797 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sharahil ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, who said: I heard Muawiyah addressing upon the minbar, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17882","Abu Said al-Maqburi from Muawiyah. 798 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from his father, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying upon the minbar, with a lock of hair in his hand: What is wrong with your women putting upon their heads the like of this? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no woman who puts upon her head hair from other than her own hair except that it is falsehood."
"17883","799 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17884","Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Muawiyah. 800 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, that he heard Muawiyah upon the minbar, with a bun of womens buns with him, saying: What is wrong with Muslim women doing this? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who adds to her head hair that is not of it, it is falsehood."
"17885","Muslim ibn Hurmuz from Muawiyah. 801 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will always remain in this ummah a people fighting upon the command of Allah; the enmity of those who oppose them will not harm them, nor the abandonment of those who forsake them, until the command of Allah Almighty comes to them while they are upon that."
"17886","Ibn Yasaf from Muawiyah. 802 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Suri al-Nahwi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Ibn Yasaf, that he heard Muawiyah narrating that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever hears the muadhdhin and says the like of what he says shall have the like of his reward."
"17887","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj from Muawiyah. 803 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yaqub narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Sad, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"17888","Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of Uthman, from Muawiyah. 804 - Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Hudhayfah ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of the family of Uthman, who said: The muadhdhin gave the adhan and said: Allahu Akbar, so Muawiyah said: Allahu Akbar; then the muadhdhin said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, so Muawiyah said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; then the muadhdhin said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, so Muawiyah said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then Muawiyah said: This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17889","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz from Muawiyah. 805 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, who said: I heard Muawiyah, while upon the minbar in Medina, saying: O people of Medina, where are your jurists? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the like of this lock, and he placed it upon his head; I never saw it upon a bride nor upon any other more beautiful than upon Muawiyah."
"17890","806 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan upon the minbar, mentioning the day of Ashura, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The day of Ashura, we used to fast it in the Age of Ignorance, then Allah obligated upon us the fast of Ramadan, so He lifted from us the fast of Ashura; whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may break it."
"17891","Mujahid from Muawiyah. 807 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Huraysh narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mujahid, who said: I heard Mujahid saying: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hasten toward something thinking that if you hasten to it you will attain it though Allah has not decreed it for you, nor delay from something thinking that if you delay from it you have escaped it though Allah has decreed it upon you."
"17892","Hammam ibn Munabbih from Muawiyah. 808 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Wahb ibn Munabbih saying in Sanaa, and he fed me from a walnut in his house, narrating from his brother, from Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not press insistently in asking; for by Allah, none of you asks me for anything, and asking extracts it from me so I give it to him while I dislike it for him, and then he is blessed in what I gave him."
"17893","809 - Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Harun ibn Said al-Ayli narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from his brother, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man asks me for something and I withhold it so that you may intercede and be rewarded."
"17894","Yusuf ibn Mahak from Muawiyah. 810 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Harun ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Akhnas, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17895","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Muawiyah. 811 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ubaydah ibn Hassan, from Ata, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me not to approach my family on the first night of the crescent, not to perform ablution in a copper vessel, and to clean my teeth every time I rise from my sleep."
"17896","Abdullah ibn Ali from Muawiyah. 812 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Harithi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to me, that his father informed him, saying: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding wearing gold and silk."
"17897","Among those who narrated from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan from the people of Basra: Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Muawiyah. 813 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who heard Mutarrif narrating from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying concerning Laylat al-Qadr: Twenty-seven."
"17898","814 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from Said al-Harrani, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the night of the twenty-seventh."
"17899","Mabad al-Juhani from Muawiyah. 815 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, saying: I heard Mabad saying: Muawiyah rarely narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he would mention these words, often narrating them in the Friday sermons: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion; and this wealth is green and sweet, so whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it; and beware of excessive praise, for it is slaughter."
"17900","816 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Mabad al-Juhani, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The world is sweet and green; whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it."
"17901","817 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Mabad al-Juhani, who said: Muawiyah rarely narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said in his sermon: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Beware of excessive praise, for it is slaughter."
"17902","818 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar, Bundar, narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Mabad al-Juhani, from Muawiyah, who said: You pray this prayer; we accompanied the Messenger of Allah and saw him, and we never saw him pray this prayer after the prayer, meaning Asr."
"17903","Abu Mijlaz Lahiq ibn Humayd from Muawiyah. 819 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, that Muawiyah entered a house in which were Abdullah ibn Amir and Ibn al-Zubayr; Ibn al-Zubayr sat while Abdullah ibn Amir stood, and he was the weightier of the two men; so Muawiyah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is pleased that men stand before him, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"17904","820 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Abu Mijlaz, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is pleased that men stand before him, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"17905","821 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Abu Mijlaz, from Muawiyah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that people stand before him, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"17906","822 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Hayyan ibn Musa al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Abu Mijlaz, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is pleased that men stand before him, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"17907","823 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from Imran ibn Hudayr, from Abu Mijlaz, that Muawiyah said: Leveling graves is from the sunnah, while the Jews and Christians raised them, so do not imitate them."
"17908","Abu Shaykh al-Hunai from Muawiyah. 824 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, that Muawiyah said to a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in vessels of gold and silver? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding upon tiger skins? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And do you know that he forbade mutah, meaning the mutah of Hajj? They said: O Allah, no. He said: Yes indeed."
"17909","825 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, who said: I was among a gathering of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Muawiyah, and Muawiyah said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in vessels of gold and silver? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness."
"17910","826 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, who said: I heard Muawiyah, with a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with him, saying: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk? They said: O Allah, yes."
"17911","827 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, that Muawiyah said one day, with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with him: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold except in small pieces? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding upon leopard skins? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining Hajj and Umrah? They said: O Allah, no."
"17912","828 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, from Qatadah, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17913","829 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Bayhas ibn Fahdan narrated to us, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, who said: I was with Muawiyah, with people from the Muhajirun and Ansar with him, and Muawiyah said: I adjure you by Allah, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold except in small pieces? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in silver vessels? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining Hajj and Umrah? They said: O Allah, yes."
"17914","Himman, brother of Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, from Muawiyah. 830 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Shuayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Shaykh al-Hunai narrated to me, Himman narrated to me, saying: Muawiyah performed Hajj and invited a group of the Ansar, saying: I adjure you by Allah, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding rows of silk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbids rows of tiger skins? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness."
"17915","831 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Fayyad al-Zammani narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Shaykh narrated to him, from his brother Himman, that he witnessed Muawiyah, with people from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with him, saying: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold except in small pieces? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding upon leopard skins? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness."
"17916","832 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Shaykh narrated to me, Himman narrated to me, saying: Muawiyah performed Hajj and invited a group of the Ansar in the Kabah, saying: I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding gold? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade rows of tiger skins? They said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness. Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade silk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness."
"17917","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Muawiyah. 833 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Sarrar ibn Mujashshir Abu Ubaydah al-Anazi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: When Muawiyah pledged allegiance to Yazid, he performed Hajj, passed by Medina, and addressed the people, saying: We have pledged allegiance to Yazid, so pledge allegiance. Then al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: I am, by Allah, more deserving of it than he; my father is better than his father, my grandfather is better than his grandfather, my mother is better than his mother, and I am better than he. So Muawiyah said: As for what you mentioned that your grandfather is better than his grandfather, you spoke truly; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is better than Abu Sufyan ibn Harb. And as for what you mentioned that your mother is better than his mother, you spoke truly; Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is better than the daughter of Majdal. And as for what you mentioned that your father is better than his father, his father contended with your father, and Allah decreed for his father over your father. And as for what you mentioned that you are better than he, he is indeed more forbearing than you and more intelligent; nothing would please me in exchange for him like a thousand of you."
"17918","Muharib Abu Maslamah from Muawiyah. 834 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, Awn ibn Kahmas narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from his father, who said: Muawiyah wrote to Ziyad that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The enemy does not prevail over a people when they - or he said: I saw them - are with a man from Banu Bakr ibn Wail."
"17919","Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan from Muawiyah. 835 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, who said: Muawiyah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Matters only increase in severity, people only increase in miserliness, and the Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."
"17920","Ayyub ibn Abdullah ibn Yasar from Muawiyah. 836 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, Abu Mashar al-Bara narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Abdullah ibn Yasar narrated to us, who said: I heard Muawiyah, while in Mecca on the day of Ashura, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted it, and said: Whoever among you has not fasted, let him fast it."
"17921","Abu Qilabah al-Jarmi from Muawiyah. 837 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold except in small pieces, and riding upon leopard skins."
"17922","838 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Maymun al-Qannad, from Abu Qilabah, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding upon leopard skins, and wearing gold except in small pieces."
"17923","Abu Maymunah from Muawiyah. 839 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Abu Zayd al-Hawtiyyan narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, who said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said: The people of Mecca expelled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the caliphate shall not be among them; and the people of Medina killed Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, so the caliphate shall never return among them."
"17924","Among those who narrated from Muawiyah from the people of Kufa: Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him. 840 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Bayan, from Qays, from Muawiyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My ummah will remain dominant over people until the command of Allah comes."
"17925","Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from Muawiyah. 841 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ashari, who said: I entered upon Muawiyah while he was writhing, with an ulcer between his shoulders, and he said: Nothing would please me more than not feeling what you see. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No harm afflicts the believer in his body except that it is an expiation for his sins."
"17926","842 - Abu Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wadii al-Qadi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, who said: I entered upon Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, with an ulcer on his back, groaning from it with severe groaning, and I said: Is all this from this? He said: Nothing would please me more than that this groaning had not been. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim is afflicted with harm in his body except that it is an expiation for his sins; and this is the severest of harm."
"17927","Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, whose name is Mabad ibn Mabad, and it is said: Abd ibn Abd, and it is said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd, from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him. 843 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Abd ibn Abd, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, beat him; if he returns, beat him; then if he returns, kill him."
"17928","844 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Jadali, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him, three times; then if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck."
"17929","845 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Hafs al-Ubulli narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Mughirah, from Mabad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Jadali, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him; then if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck."
"17930","846 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, Hakkam ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him; then if he does it a fourth time, kill him."
"17931","Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl from Muawiyah. 847 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, who said: Muawiyah wrote to Amr: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Quraysh are the guardians of people in good and evil until the Day of Resurrection."
"17932","Amr ibn Yahya al-Qurashi from Muawiyah. 848 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Qurashi, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed those who split speeches as poetry is split."
"17933","Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani from Muawiyah. 849 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever supplicates with these five words, Allah will not be asked for anything except that He gives it to him: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable; there is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"17934","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Muawiyah. 850 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, who said: Muawiyah said: I never ceased hoping for the caliphate since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If you rule, then rule well."
"17935","Man ibn Ali from Muawiyah. 851 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Hilal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Iyad ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Fayyad, from Man ibn Ali, who said: I prayed with Muawiyah, the Commander of the Believers, and he stood in the second rakah, so the people said Subhan Allah to him, and he gestured to them with his hand to stand; then when he finished his prayer he prostrated two prostrations for that, then departed, saying: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"17936","Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami from Muawiyah. 852 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, al-Mughirah Abu Salamah al-Khurasani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, that Muawiyah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that the children of Adam stand before him, the Fire becomes due for him."
"17937","853 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best of you to their families."
"17938","854 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf al-Jubari narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to a gathered company and said: What has gathered you? They said: We remember Allah and what He has bestowed upon us, and how He rescued us through Him from ignorance and its folly. He said: By Allah, is it for that that you gathered? They said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you are truthful, Allah Almighty boasts of you to the angels."
"17939","Abu Umayyah al-Thaqafi from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan. 855 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Umayyah al-Thaqafi, who said: Muawiyah came out after praying Zuhr and said: Stay in your places until I come to you; then he came out to us having wrapped himself, and when he prayed Asr he said: Shall I not narrate to you something done by the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They prayed the first prayer with him, then sat; then he came out to them and said: Have you not yet departed? They said: No. He said: If you could see your Lord opening a door of heaven, showing your gathering to His angels, boasting of you while you await the prayer."
"17940","Among those who narrated from Muawiyah from the people of Sham: Abu Idris al-Khawlani from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him. 856 - Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih al-Jurjusi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Isa ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Awf al-Ansari, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, who heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no sin except that Allah may forgive it, except one who was a polytheist or killed a believer deliberately."
"17941","857 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, Abu Awn narrated to us, that Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrated to them that Muawiyah said - and he rarely narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every sin may be forgiven except that a man dies while a disbeliever, or kills a believer deliberately."
"17942","858 - Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abu Awn, from Abu Idris, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every sin may Allah forgive except a man who dies a disbeliever, or a man who kills a believer deliberately."
"17943","Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Muawiyah. 859 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, Yahya ibn Jabir narrated to us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him that his father narrated to him that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I heard words from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by which Allah benefited me; I heard him say: Turn away from people; have you not seen that if you pursue suspicion among people you corrupt them, or nearly corrupt them?"
"17944","Abdullah ibn Muhayriz al-Jumahi from Muawiyah. 860 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17945","861 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The hearing obedient one has no argument against him, and the hearing disobedient one has no excuse."
"17946","862 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me. And al-Husayn ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, all of them from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz al-Jumahi, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O people, do not race me to bowing and prostration; whatever I precede you in, when I bow you will catch me in it when I rise; I have grown stout, that is, I have grown old. And the wording is that of the hadith of Sulayman ibn Bilal."
"17947","863 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Ibn Muhayriz al-Jumahi, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do not race me in bowing and prostration, for whatever I precede you in when I prostrate, you will catch me in it when I rise; and whatever I precede you in when I bow, you will catch me in it when I rise; and I have grown stout."
"17948","Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Muawiyah. 864 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Dawud, from Abu Asma, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17949","Ubadah ibn Nusayy al-Kindi from Muawiyah. 865 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Abdullah ibn Sad, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy al-Kindi, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that they mentioned difficult questions in his presence, whereupon he said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade knotty questions."
"17950","Ubaydah ibn al-Muhajir Abu Abd Rabb from Muawiyah. 866 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed us, Abu Abd Rabb narrated to us, saying: I heard Muawiyah saying upon the minbar: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There remains of this world only trial and tribulation; and the likeness of each of you is that of a vessel: when its top is good, its bottom is good."
"17951","867 - Abu Imran Musa ibn Sahl al-Khawlani narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jabir narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn al-Muhajir Abu Abd Rabb narrated to us, that he heard Muawiyah upon the minbar narrating that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man was extravagant against himself, then came to a man and said: The other killed ninety-nine souls, all of them killing them unjustly, so is there repentance for me? He said: No, so he killed him; then he came to another and said: The other killed a hundred souls, all of them unjustly, so is there repentance for him? He said: If I tell you that Allah does not accept the repentance of one who repents, I have lied to you; over there is a place wherein are a people who worship, so go to them and worship Allah with them. So he set out toward them and died upon that; then the angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed, so Allah sent to them an angel who said: Measure between the two places, and whichever he was closer to, he is of them; so they found him closer to the monastery of the repentant by a finger-breadth, and he was forgiven. And the wording is that of the hadith of al-Walid."
"17952","868 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sasaah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Thawban, from Abu Abd Rabb, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah is not outwitted, nor deceived, nor informed of what He does not know; whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17953","Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi al-Qari from Muawiyah. 869 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi, who said: I heard Muawiyah upon the minbar in Damascus saying: O people, beware of the narrations of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except a narration that was mentioned in the time of Umar, for Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was a man who struck fear into people concerning Allah. Then I heard him saying: Verily I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17954","Verily, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am only a keeper, and it is Allah who gives; so whomever I give out of contentment of soul, it is blessed for him in it; and whomever I give a gift upon asking, he is like one who eats and is not satiated."
"17955","Verily, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain a community from my ummah standing upon the command of Allah; those who oppose them will not harm them, nor those who forsake them, until Allah comes while they are dominant over people."
"17956","870 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will always stand with the truth, fighting those who fight them and war against them until the Day of Resurrection."
"17957","871 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17958","872 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am only a keeper, and it is Allah who gives; so whomever I give a gift while I am content in soul over it, it is blessed for him in it; and whomever I give a gift out of greed of soul and insistence of asking, he is like one who eats and is not satiated."
"17959","873 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amir, that he heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the minbar: I am only a keeper, and it is Allah who gives; so whomever I give a gift while my soul is content with it, it is blessed for him in it; and whomever I give a gift out of greed of soul and insistence of asking, he is like one who eats and is not satiated."
"17960","Ibn Hubayrah from Muawiyah. 874 - Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, al-Hasan ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Ibn Hubayrah, that he was speaking with Muawiyah when the muadhdhin gave the adhan, so he ordered him to listen quietly; then he said Allahu Akbar as he said Allahu Akbar; then the muadhdhin said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, so he said: And we bear witness that there is no god but Allah. The muadhdhin said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, so he said: And we bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Ibn Hubayrah said: So I said to him: Is it something you saw, or did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say Allahu Akbar when he heard the muadhdhin; then when he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, he said: And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; and when he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, he said: And I bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah."
"17961","Atiyyah ibn Qays al-Kilabi from Muawiyah. 875 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn al-Samaydi al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us. And Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The eye is the tie of the rear; when the eye sleeps, the tie comes loose; so whoever sleeps, let him perform ablution."
"17962","Kaysan Abu Hariz, freedman of Muawiyah, from Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him. 876 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abu Hariz, freedman of Muawiyah, who said: Muawiyah addressed the people and mentioned in his sermon: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade six things, and I convey them to you and forbid you from them: among them wailing, poetry, images, immodest display, skins of predators, gold, and silk."
"17963","877 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir al-Ansari narrated to us, from Kaysan, freedman of Muawiyah, who said: Muawiyah addressed the people and said: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nine things, and I forbid you from them: wailing, poetry, immodest display, images, skins of predators, singing, gold, fornication, and silk."
"17964","878 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Habban al-Raqqi narrated to us, both saying: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Kaysan, freedman of Muawiyah, who said: Muawiyah addressed us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nine things, and I forbid you from them; verily among them are: wailing, singing, images, poetry, gold, fornication, saddles, and silk."
"17965","Al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman from Muawiyah. 879 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me, al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, saying: I was sitting with Muawiyah when he sent for Abdullah ibn Amr and said: What narrations have reached me from you that you narrate? I was about to exile you from Sham. He said: By Allah, were it not for womenfolk I would not like to be in it for an hour. Then Muawiyah said: What narration do you narrate concerning intoxicants? He said: It is not lawful for me to say upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say; I heard him say: Whoever attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say concerning wine: Whoever places it upon his palm, his supplication is not accepted; and whoever persists in drinking it will be given to drink from al-Khabal, and al-Khabal is a valley in Hell. He said: O Muawiyah, I see you have heard the like of what I heard. He said: Then Muawiyah was about to affirm him, then fell silent."
"17966","880 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, that he heard Muawiyah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand upon the minbar a day before Ramadan and say: Fasting is on such-and-such day; we are going ahead, so whoever wishes to go ahead, let him go ahead; and whoever wishes to leave it, let him leave it."
"17967","Ibn Dhi al-Kala from Muawiyah. 881 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Hassan ibn Kurayb narrated to us, that he heard Ibn Dhi Kala saying: I was with Muawiyah when he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will conquer the growing places of wormwood."
"17968","882 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Kab ibn Alqamah al-Tanukhi, Hassan ibn Kurayb narrated to me, saying: I heard Ibn Dhi al-Kala saying: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Leave the Turks as long as they leave you."
"17969","883 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Kab ibn Alqamah, who said: I heard Hassan ibn Kurayb al-Himyari saying: I heard Ibn Dhi Kala saying: A courier came to Muawiyah from the chief of Armenia; when Muawiyah read the letter he came out angry, then called his scribe and said: Write to the chief of Armenia in reply to his letter: May your mother be bereft of you, and do not provoke them in anything, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Leave the Turks as long as they leave you."
"17970","Abu Amir al-Hawzani Abdullah ibn Luhayy from Muawiyah. 884 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us. And Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, both saying: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Azhar ibn Abdullah, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani Abdullah ibn Luhayy, who said: We performed Hajj with Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan; when we arrived in Mecca he was informed of a storyteller narrating to the people of Mecca, a freedman of Banu Makhzum; so Muawiyah sent for him and said: Were you commanded with this storytelling? He said: No. He said: What carried you to narrate without permission? He said: We spread knowledge that Allah taught us. Then Muawiyah said: Had I warned you before this time of mine, I would have cut off a piece of you. Then he stood until he prayed Zuhr in Mecca, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The People of the Book split into seventy-two sects, and this ummah will split into seventy-three sects - meaning desires - all of them in the Fire except one, and it is the Jamaah. And he said: There will emerge from my ummah peoples whom desires will course through as rabies courses through its victim, leaving no vein nor joint except entering it. By Allah, O assembly of Arabs, if you do not uphold what Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought, others among people are even less likely to uphold it."
"17971","885 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to me, from al-Azhar ibn Abdullah al-Hawzani, from Abu Amir Abdullah ibn Luhayy al-Hawzani, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The People of the Book split in their book into seventy-two sects, and this ummah will split into seventy-three sects - meaning desires - all of them in the Fire except one, and it is the Jamaah; and there will emerge in my ummah peoples through whom those desires will course as rabies courses through its victim, leaving no vein nor joint except entering it."
"17972","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi from Muawiyah. 886 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mundhir, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi, that Muawiyah showed them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he reached wiping the head, he placed his palms upon the front of his head, then carried them until reaching the nape, then returned them until reaching the place from which he began."
"17973","887 - Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn al-Mundhir said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi narrating from Muawiyah: that he showed them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he reached wiping the head, he placed his palms upon the front of his head, then passed them until reaching the nape, then returned them until reaching the place from which he began. Al-Walid said: And Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr informed me, from Abu al-Azhar, from Muawiyah, with the like of that. And Hariz ibn Uthman informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"17974","888 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Muhammad, al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi narrated to me, that he was present when Muawiyah performed ablution and wiped his ears, their outer and inner, saying: This is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17975","Yazid ibn Abi Malik and Abu al-Azhar from Muawiyah. 889 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala narrated to me, that Yazid ibn Abi Malik and Abu al-Azhar narrated to him concerning the ablution of Muawiyah, showing them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he performed ablution three times, except washing his feet without count."
"17976","Rashid ibn Sad from Muawiyah. 890 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Muawiyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If you pursue the faults of people, you corrupt them, or nearly corrupt them. He said: Abu al-Darda says: A word which Muawiyah heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by which Allah benefited him."
"17977","891 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us. And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to me, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Rashid ibn Sad al-Maqrai, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he used to teach people the tashahhud upon the minbar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"17978","Al-Sunabihi from Muawiyah. 892 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sad, from al-Sunabihi, from Muawiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ghalutat. Ishaq said: And Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from al-Awzai, who said: And ghalutat are difficult questions and hard ones."
"17979","Ubayd ibn Sad and Ibn Abi Maryam from Muawiyah. 893 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi al-Qadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamir al-Uruqi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Idris al-Uswari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, Asim ibn Raja ibn Haywah narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Sad and Ibn Abi Maryam, that they heard Muawiyah upon the minbar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain from my ummah a community standing; those who forsake them will not harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are dominant over people."
"17980","Thabit ibn Sad from Muawiyah. 894 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Tai narrated to us, Thabit ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hold upon truthfulness, for it guides to righteousness, and both are in Paradise; and beware of lying, for it guides to wickedness, and both are in the Fire."
"17981","Malik ibn Yakhamir from Muawiyah (895) — Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Malik ibn Yakhamir al-Saksaki, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hijrah (emigration) is of two kinds: one is to abandon evil deeds, and the other is to emigrate to Allah and His Messenger. Hijrah does not cease as long as repentance is accepted, and repentance continues to be accepted until the sun rises from the west; when it rises, every heart is sealed according to what is in it and people are relieved of (further) deeds."
"17982","Umayr ibn al-Harith al-Sakuni from Muawiyah (896) — Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother, from Ibn Aidh, from Umayr ibn al-Harith al-Sakuni, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and listened to him, and I heard that most of his prayer was his saying: Glory be to You, Lord of the worlds."
"17983","Abd Allah ibn Mawhab from Muawiyah (897) — Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, that Ibn Mawhab informed him that he was with Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan when Marwan came in to him and spoke to him about his needs, saying: Fulfil my need, O Commander of the Faithful, for by Allah my burden is great; I have become a father of ten, a brother of ten, and an uncle of ten. When Marwan turned away while Ibn Abbas was sitting with Muawiyah on his couch, Muawiyah said: I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sons of al-Hakam reach thirty men they will take the signs of Allah as spoils among themselves, His servants as bondsmen, and His Book as a deceit; and when they reach four hundred and ninety-nine, their destruction will be swifter than the fruit (falling)? Ibn Abbas said: O Allah, yes. Then Marwan mentioned a need of his, and Marwan ibn Abd al-Malik returned to Muawiyah and spoke to him about it; when he turned away, Muawiyah said: I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned this one and said: The father of the four tyrants? Ibn Abbas said: O Allah, yes."
"17984","Abu Abd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam from Muawiyah (898) — Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad al-Ma'na narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Abd Allah who said: I heard Muawiyah on the pulpit — and he narrated little from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted brought forth the offspring of Adam from his loins until they filled the earth, and they were like this — and Jafar clasped his hands, one over the other."
"17985","Umayr ibn Hani al-Ansi from Muawiyah (899) — Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me that Umayr ibn Hani narrated to him that he heard Muawiyah say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain a group of my ummah upholding the command of Allah; those who forsake them will not harm them until the command of Allah comes while they are dominant over people."
"17986","Abu al-Azhar from Muawiyah (900) — Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani and Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, both saying: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Abu al-Azhar, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he described to them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he wiped his head until water dripped from his head or almost dripped, and that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the wiping of his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head then passed them over it until he reached the nape with them, then returned them until he reached the place from which he had begun."
"17987","(901) — Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu al-Azhar say: Muawiyah stood at Dayr Mishaal which is at the gate of Hims and said: Indeed the fast is on such-and-such day, and we shall proceed tomorrow. Malik ibn Hubayrah stood up to him and said: O Muawiyah, is it an opinion you hold or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fast the month and its end (or: its secret)."
"17988","Ayyub ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas from Muawiyah (902) — Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Maysarah, from Muawiyah, that he used to send guards from among his guards to Kanakirun Kabbah, and they would stand and say: This is the day of Ashura, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast it, and we are fasting; whoever wishes to fast it, let him fast it."
"17989","Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas from Muawiyah (903) — Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Muawiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No ummah is sanctified in which judgment is not passed with truth and the weak takes his right from the strong without stammering (without fear)."
"17990","(904) — Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us (H). And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us — they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Marwan ibn Janah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Maysarah narrated to us, saying: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Goodness is a habit and evil is obstinacy. Ibn bint Shurahbil added in his hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17991","(905) — Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Marwan ibn Janah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: We were sitting in the mosque when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us (saying): You are saying that I am among the last of you to die and that I am among the first of you to die, and you will follow me in scattered groups — meaning some of you after others — then he drew evidence with this verse, saying: {Say: He is Able to send upon you punishment from above you or from beneath your feet} — until he reached: {For every announcement there is an appointed time, and you shall come to know} — then he said: There will always remain a band of my ummah fighting upon the truth, dominant, not caring who forsakes them nor who opposes them until the command of Allah comes upon that. Then he drew evidence with this verse: {O Isa, I shall take you and raise you to Me and purify you from those who disbelieved, and make those who followed you above those who disbelieved until the Day of Resurrection}."
"17992","(906) — Al-Husayn ibn al-Samayda al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas narrated to us, saying: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"17993","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Do you say that I am among the last of you to die? We said: Yes. He said: I am among the first of you to die, then you will follow me in scattered groups, some of you following others."
"17994","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain a group of my ummah established upon the truth, not caring who opposes them nor who forsakes them until the command of Allah comes while they are dominant over people."
"17995","Abu Hind al-Bajali from Muawiyah (907) — Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Awf narrated to me, from Abu Hind al-Bajali, from Muawiyah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Hijrah does not cease until repentance ceases — three times — and repentance does not cease until the sun rises from its west."
"17996","Rabiah ibn Yazid from Muawiyah (908) — Abd al-Aziz ibn Sulayman al-Harmali al-Antaki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Kab narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, that Muawiyah wrote to Maslamah ibn Makhlad: Ask Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As whether he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No ummah is sanctified in which its weak does not take his right from its strong while he is not oppressed? If he says yes, then carry him to me by post — so he asked him and he said: Yes. So he carried him by post from Egypt to Syria, and Muawiyah asked him and he informed him, and Muawiyah said: I too have heard it, but I wished to verify it."
"17997","Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws from Muawiyah (909) — Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather (H). And Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Yala ibn Shaddad, Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed every intoxicant is forbidden upon every believer."
"17998","Shurayh ibn Ubayd from Muawiyah (910) — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Muawiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies without an imam dies a death of ignorance."
"17999","Raja ibn Haywah from Muawiyah (911) — Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jarad, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"18000","(912) — Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Muawiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah intends good for, let him seek understanding of the religion."
